1
00:00:02,139 --> 00:00:05,540
I wanted to be weak, that I might avoid the awful

2
00:00:05,542 --> 00:00:08,519
passage of further suffering I saw laid out for me.

3
00:00:09,379 --> 00:00:15,819
And conscience turned tyrant, held passion by the throat, told her tauntingly.

4
00:00:16,599 --> 00:00:21,660
She had yet, but dipped her dainty foot in the slough, and swore that with that arm

5
00:00:21,661 --> 00:00:26,099
of iron he would thrust her down to unsounded depths of agony.

6
00:00:27,260 --> 00:00:31,860
Let me be torn away then, I cried, let another help me.

7
00:00:32,739 --> 00:00:37,440
No, you shall tear yourself away, none shall help you, you shall yourself

8
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:41,506
pluck out your right eye, yourself cut off your right hand, your

9
00:00:41,506 --> 00:00:46,360
heart shall be the victim, and you the priest to transfix it.

10
00:00:48,059 --> 00:00:53,980
I rose up suddenly, terror struck at the solitude, which so ruthless a judge

11
00:00:53,980 --> 00:00:58,500
haunted, at the silence which so awful a voice filled.

12
00:00:59,639 --> 00:01:02,440
My head swam as I stood erect.

13
00:01:03,500 --> 00:01:06,680
I perceived that I was sickening from excitement and in addition.

14
00:01:07,959 --> 00:01:12,019
Neither meat nor drink had passed my lips that day, for I had taken no breakfast.

15
00:01:13,339 --> 00:01:19,199
And with a strange pang, I now reflected that, long as I had been shut up here,

16
00:01:20,019 --> 00:01:25,919
no message had been sent to ask how I was, or to invite me to come down.

17
00:01:26,959 --> 00:01:29,339
Not even little Adele had tapped at the door.

18
00:01:30,220 --> 00:01:32,260
Not even Mrs. Fairfax had sought me.

19
00:01:33,620 --> 00:01:36,879
Friends always forget those whom fortune forsakes.

20
00:01:37,800 --> 00:01:40,980
I murmured as I undrew the bolt and passed out.

21
00:01:42,080 --> 00:01:43,699
I stumbled over an obstacle.

22
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:49,339
My head was still dizzy, my sight was dim, and my limbs were feeble.

23
00:01:50,040 --> 00:01:51,379
I could not soon recover myself.

24
00:01:51,959 --> 00:01:54,300
I fell, but not onto the ground.

25
00:01:55,040 --> 00:01:56,739
An outstretched arm caught me.

26
00:01:57,419 --> 00:01:58,419
I looked up.

27
00:01:58,860 --> 00:02:03,260
I was supported by Mr. Rochester, who sat in a chair across my chamber threshold.

28
00:02:03,860 --> 00:02:06,760
You come out at last, he said.

29
00:02:07,720 --> 00:02:10,993
Well, I have been waiting for you long and listening,

30
00:02:10,995 --> 00:02:14,300
yet not one movement have I heard, nor one sob.

31
00:02:15,099 --> 00:02:17,472
Five minutes more of that death-like hush, and

32
00:02:17,472 --> 00:02:20,701
I should have forced the lock like a burglar.

33
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:22,019
So you shunned me?

34
00:02:22,639 --> 00:02:24,660
You shut yourself up and grieve alone.

35
00:02:25,419 --> 00:02:28,980
I would rather you had come and upgraded me with vehemence.

36
00:02:29,680 --> 00:02:30,680
You are passionate.

37
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:33,419
I expected a scene of some kind.

38
00:02:34,019 --> 00:02:36,326
I was prepared for the hot rain of tears,

39
00:02:36,328 --> 00:02:39,841
only I wanted them to be shared on my breast.

40
00:02:40,440 --> 00:02:44,019
Now a senseless floor has received them, or your drenched hankerchief.

41
00:02:44,800 --> 00:02:45,800
But I err.

42
00:02:46,300 --> 00:02:47,879
You have not wept at all.

43
00:02:48,739 --> 00:02:52,660
I see a white cheek and a faded eye, but no trace of tears.

44
00:02:53,620 --> 00:02:56,959
I suppose then your heart has been weeping blood.

45
00:02:57,839 --> 00:03:02,620
Well, Jane, not a word of reproach, nothing bitter, nothing poignant,

46
00:03:03,239 --> 00:03:05,500
nothing to cut a feeling, or sting a passion.

47
00:03:06,300 --> 00:03:11,160
You sit quietly where I have placed you, and regard me with a weary, passive look.

48
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:16,120
Jane, I never meant to wound you thus.

49
00:03:17,040 --> 00:03:21,959
If the man who had but one little you lamb that was dear to him as a daughter,

50
00:03:22,580 --> 00:03:27,839
that ate of his bread and drank of his cup, and lay in his bosom, had by some

51
00:03:27,841 --> 00:03:31,567
mistake slaughtered it at the shambles, he would not

52
00:03:31,569 --> 00:03:34,879
have rude his bloody blunder more than I now room mine.

53
00:03:35,580 --> 00:03:37,160
Will you ever forgive me?

54
00:03:37,919 --> 00:03:41,980
Reader, I forgave him at the moment and on the spot.

55
00:03:43,720 --> 00:03:49,980
There was such deep remorse in his eye, such true pity in his tone, such manly

56
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:52,891
energy in his manner, and besides, there was

57
00:03:52,892 --> 00:03:56,080
such unchanged love in his whole look and men.

58
00:03:56,639 --> 00:04:02,559
I forgave him all, yet not in words, not outwardly, only at my heart's core.

59
00:04:04,080 --> 00:04:06,080
You know I am a scoundrel, Jane?

60
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:11,760
Air long he inquired wistfully, wondering, I suppose, at my continued

61
00:04:11,760 --> 00:04:15,839
silence and tameness, the result rather of weakness than of will.

62
00:04:17,220 --> 00:04:22,019
Yes, sir, then tell me so roundly and sharply, don't spare me.

63
00:04:22,919 --> 00:04:26,860
I cannot, I am tired and sick, I want some water.

64
00:04:27,959 --> 00:04:33,760
He heaved a sort of shuddering sigh and taking me in his arms, carried me downstairs.

65
00:04:34,480 --> 00:04:37,353
At first I did not know to what room he had

66
00:04:37,355 --> 00:04:41,241
borne me, all was cloudy to my glazed sight.

67
00:04:41,639 --> 00:04:44,660
Presently, I felt the reviving warmth of a fire.

68
00:04:45,379 --> 00:04:50,180
For, summer as it was, I had become icy cold in my chamber.

69
00:04:50,919 --> 00:04:54,703
He put wine to my lips, I tasted it and revived, then

70
00:04:54,703 --> 00:04:58,300
I ate something he offered me and was soon myself.

71
00:04:59,059 --> 00:05:02,540
I was in the library, sitting in his chair, he was quite near.

72
00:05:04,019 --> 00:05:07,705
If I could go out of life now, without too sharp

73
00:05:07,705 --> 00:05:10,699
a pang, it would be well for me, I thought.

74
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:15,769
Then I should not have to make the effort of cracking my

75
00:05:15,769 --> 00:05:19,220
heartstrings in rending them from among Mr. Rochester's.

76
00:05:19,739 --> 00:05:21,900
I must leave him, it appears.

77
00:05:22,720 --> 00:05:25,620
I do not want to leave him, I cannot leave him.

78
00:05:27,180 --> 00:05:28,519
How are you now, Jane?

79
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Much better, sir.

80
00:05:31,680 --> 00:05:32,760
I shall be well soon.

81
00:05:34,059 --> 00:05:35,139
Taste the wine again, Jane.

82
00:05:36,779 --> 00:05:37,800
I obeyed him.

83
00:05:39,040 --> 00:05:44,940
Then he put the glass on the table, stood before me, and looked at me attentively.

84
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:49,377
Suddenly he turned away, with an inarticulate

85
00:05:49,379 --> 00:05:52,559
exclamation, full of passionate emotion of some kind.

86
00:05:53,199 --> 00:05:55,580
He walked fast through the room and came back.

87
00:05:56,300 --> 00:05:58,580
He stooped towards me as if to kiss me.

88
00:05:59,360 --> 00:06:01,800
But I remembered caresses were now forbidden.

89
00:06:02,500 --> 00:06:04,819
I turned my face away and put his aside.

90
00:06:05,779 --> 00:06:06,779
What?

91
00:06:07,019 --> 00:06:08,019
How is this?

92
00:06:08,500 --> 00:06:09,779
He exclaimed hastily.

93
00:06:11,120 --> 00:06:12,120
Oh, I know.

94
00:06:12,860 --> 00:06:14,959
You won't kiss the husband of birthamason.

95
00:06:15,900 --> 00:06:23,900
You consider my arms filled and my room nor claim for me, sir.

96
00:06:25,059 --> 00:06:26,059
Why, Jane?

97
00:06:26,360 --> 00:06:28,440
I will spare you the trouble of much talking.

98
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:32,860
I will answer for you, because I have a wife already you would reply.

99
00:06:34,099 --> 00:06:35,120
I guess rightly.

100
00:06:36,180 --> 00:06:40,699
Yes, if you think so, you must have a strange opinion of me.

101
00:06:41,139 --> 00:06:45,459
You must regard me as a plotting profligate, a base and low rake who has

102
00:06:45,461 --> 00:06:49,680
been simulating disinterested love in order to draw you into a snare

103
00:06:49,680 --> 00:06:55,099
deliberately laid, and strip you of honor, and rob you of self-respect.

104
00:06:56,779 --> 00:06:58,239
What do you say to that?

105
00:06:59,699 --> 00:07:01,019
I see you can say nothing.

106
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:06,599
In the first place you are faint still, and have enough to do to draw your breath.

107
00:07:07,400 --> 00:07:12,620
In the second place you cannot yet accustom yourself to accuse and revile me.

108
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:16,622
And besides, the floodgates of tears are opened,

109
00:07:16,624 --> 00:07:19,821
and they would rush out if you spoke much.

110
00:07:20,239 --> 00:07:25,260
And you have no desire to expostulate, to upgrade, to make a scene.

111
00:07:26,199 --> 00:07:30,120
You are thinking how to act, talking you consider is of no use.

112
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:31,900
I know you.

113
00:07:32,300 --> 00:07:33,300
I am on my guard.

114
00:07:34,779 --> 00:07:41,519
Sir, I do not wish to act against you, I said, and my unsteady voice warned me to

115
00:07:41,521 --> 00:07:44,447
curtail my sentence, not in your sense of the

116
00:07:44,447 --> 00:07:48,021
word, but in mine you are scheming to destroy me.

117
00:07:48,569 --> 00:07:51,599
You have, as good as said, that I am a married man.

118
00:07:52,080 --> 00:07:55,940
As a married man you will shun me, keep out of my way.

119
00:07:56,739 --> 00:07:59,000
Just now you have refused to kiss me.

120
00:08:00,139 --> 00:08:03,675
You intend to make yourself a complete stranger to

121
00:08:03,677 --> 00:08:07,879
me, to live under this roof only as a del's governess.

122
00:08:08,900 --> 00:08:14,339
If ever I say a friendly word to you, if ever a friendly feeling inclines you

123
00:08:14,341 --> 00:08:19,040
again to me, you will say that man had nearly made me his mistress.

124
00:08:19,900 --> 00:08:21,980
I must be ice and rock to him.

125
00:08:23,379 --> 00:08:26,400
And ice and rock you will accordingly become.

126
00:08:28,000 --> 00:08:30,339
I cleared and steadied my voice to reply.

127
00:08:31,540 --> 00:08:33,260
All is changed about me, sir.

128
00:08:34,000 --> 00:08:35,000
I must change too.

129
00:08:35,440 --> 00:08:36,480
There is no doubt of that.

130
00:08:37,300 --> 00:08:40,415
And to avoid fluctuations of feeling and continual combats

131
00:08:40,417 --> 00:08:45,080
with recollections and associations, there is only one way.

132
00:08:45,919 --> 00:08:48,459
A del must have a new governess, sir.

133
00:08:49,660 --> 00:08:52,059
Oh, a del will go to school.

134
00:08:53,379 --> 00:08:54,800
I have settled that already.

135
00:08:55,779 --> 00:08:58,362
Nor do I mean to torment you with the hideous

136
00:08:58,362 --> 00:09:01,480
associations and recollections of Thornfield Hall.

137
00:09:02,279 --> 00:09:09,000
This accursed place, this tent of Akan, this insolent vault, offering the

138
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:14,919
ghastliness of living death to the light of the open sky, this narrow stone hell

139
00:09:14,921 --> 00:09:20,620
with its one real fiend, worse than a legion of such as we imagine.

140
00:09:22,139 --> 00:09:25,580
Jane, you shall not stay here, nor will I.

141
00:09:26,300 --> 00:09:31,800
I was wrong ever to bring you to Thornfield Hall, knowing as I did how it was haunted.

142
00:09:32,239 --> 00:09:38,440
I charged them to conceal from you before I ever saw you all knowledge of the curse

143
00:09:38,440 --> 00:09:44,580
of the place, merely because I feared a del never would have a governess to stay

144
00:09:44,580 --> 00:09:48,173
if she knew with what inmate she was housed, and my

145
00:09:48,173 --> 00:09:51,720
plans would not permit me to remove the maniac elsewhere.

146
00:09:53,099 --> 00:09:58,319
Though I possess an old house, ferndean manner, even more retired and

147
00:09:58,321 --> 00:10:03,540
hidden than this, where I could have lodged her safely enough, had not a

148
00:10:03,540 --> 00:10:08,260
scruple about the unhealthiness of the situation, in the heart of a wood,

149
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:11,500
made my conscience recoil from the arrangement.

150
00:10:12,500 --> 00:10:18,220
Probably those damp walls would soon have eased me of her charge, but to each

151
00:10:18,220 --> 00:10:24,000
villain his own vice, and mine is not a tendency to indirect assassination,

152
00:10:24,720 --> 00:10:26,279
even of what I most hate.

153
00:10:28,239 --> 00:10:33,059
Concealing the mad woman's neighborhood from you, however, was something like

154
00:10:33,061 --> 00:10:36,879
covering a child with a cloak and laying it down near a upa's tree.

155
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:41,559
That demon's vicinage is poisoned, and always was.

156
00:10:42,440 --> 00:10:44,419
But I'll shut up Thornfield Hall.

157
00:10:45,239 --> 00:10:47,639
I'll nail up the front door and board the lower windows.

158
00:10:48,559 --> 00:10:54,701
I'll give Mrs. Paul 200 a year to live here with my wife, as you term that fearful hag.

159
00:10:55,379 --> 00:11:00,879
Grace will do much for money, and she shall have her son, the keeper at Grimsby

160
00:11:00,881 --> 00:11:05,940
retreat, to bear her company and be at hand, to give her aid in the paroxysms,

161
00:11:06,500 --> 00:11:11,120
when my wife is prompted by her familiar, to burn people in their beds at night,

162
00:11:11,760 --> 00:11:16,319
to stab them, to bite their flesh from their bones, and so on.

163
00:11:17,580 --> 00:11:19,779
Sir, I interrupted him.

164
00:11:20,639 --> 00:11:22,839
You are inexorable for that unfortunate lady.

165
00:11:23,739 --> 00:11:26,860
You speak of her with hate, with vindictive antipathy.

166
00:11:26,860 --> 00:11:28,019
It is cruel.

167
00:11:28,459 --> 00:11:29,720
She cannot help being mad.

168
00:11:31,339 --> 00:11:35,419
Jane, my little darling, so I will call you for so you are.

169
00:11:36,239 --> 00:11:37,879
You don't know what you're talking about.

170
00:11:37,980 --> 00:11:39,120
You misjudge me again.

171
00:11:40,419 --> 00:11:42,339
It is not because she is mad.

172
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:43,580
I hate her.

173
00:11:43,760 --> 00:11:46,779
If you were mad, do you think I should hate you?

174
00:11:48,300 --> 00:11:49,739
I do indeed, sir.

175
00:11:51,120 --> 00:11:55,078
Then you are mistaken, and you know nothing about me,

176
00:11:55,078 --> 00:11:58,260
and nothing about the sort of love of which I am capable.

177
00:11:58,860 --> 00:12:03,319
Every atom of your flesh is as dear to me as my own.

178
00:12:04,019 --> 00:12:07,260
In pain and sickness, it would still be dear.

179
00:12:08,080 --> 00:12:13,940
Your mind is my treasure, and if it were broken, it would be my treasure still.

180
00:12:14,779 --> 00:12:19,671
If you raved, my arms should confine you, and not a straight

181
00:12:19,673 --> 00:12:24,440
waistcoat, your grasp even in fury would have a charm for me.

182
00:12:25,360 --> 00:12:30,220
If you flew at me as wildly as that woman did this morning, I should receive you in

183
00:12:30,220 --> 00:12:34,019
an embrace, at least as fond as it would be restrictive.

184
00:12:34,959 --> 00:12:39,139
I should not shrink from you with disgust as I did from her.

185
00:12:40,680 --> 00:12:47,559
In your quiet moments, you should have no watcher and no nurse but me, and I could

186
00:12:47,561 --> 00:12:53,199
hang over you with untiring tenderness, though you gave me no smile in return,

187
00:12:54,160 --> 00:12:57,862
and never weary of gazing into your eyes, though

188
00:12:57,864 --> 00:13:01,080
they had no longer a ray of recognition for me.

189
00:13:02,239 --> 00:13:05,101
But why do I follow that train of ideas I

190
00:13:05,101 --> 00:13:08,461
was talking of removing you from Thornfield?

191
00:13:09,300 --> 00:13:12,599
All you know is prepared for prompt departure.

192
00:13:14,220 --> 00:13:15,879
Tomorrow, you shall go.

193
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:20,970
I only ask you to endure one more night under this roof,

194
00:13:20,970 --> 00:13:24,819
Jane, and then farewell to its miseries and terrors forever.

195
00:13:24,821 --> 00:13:30,839
I have a place to repair to, which will be a secure sanctuary from hateful

196
00:13:30,841 --> 00:13:36,220
reminiscences, from unwelcome intrusion, even from falsehood and slander.

197
00:13:37,639 --> 00:13:40,620
And take Adele with you, sir, I interrupt it.

198
00:13:41,360 --> 00:13:42,940
She will be a companion for you.

199
00:13:43,739 --> 00:13:45,139
What do you mean, Jane?

200
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:50,500
I told you I would send Adele to school, and what do I want with a child for a

201
00:13:50,500 --> 00:13:54,260
companion and not my own child, a French dancer's bastard?

202
00:13:54,819 --> 00:13:57,459
Why do you importune me about her?

203
00:13:57,919 --> 00:14:01,279
I say, why do you assign Adele to me for a companion?

204
00:14:02,860 --> 00:14:08,360
You spoke of a retirement, sir, and retirement and solitude are dull,

205
00:14:08,720 --> 00:14:10,059
too dull for you.

206
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:14,339
Solitude, solitude he reiterated with irritation?

207
00:14:15,319 --> 00:14:17,699
I see I must come to an explanation.

208
00:14:18,739 --> 00:14:22,900
I don't know what this vinks like expression is forming in your countenance.

209
00:14:23,599 --> 00:14:25,279
You are to share my solitude.

210
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,220
Do you understand?

211
00:14:28,860 --> 00:14:30,080
I shook my head.

212
00:14:31,019 --> 00:14:34,853
It required a degree of courage, excited as he was

213
00:14:34,855 --> 00:14:38,160
becoming, even to risk that mute sign of dissent.

214
00:14:39,180 --> 00:14:41,692
He had been walking fast about the room and

215
00:14:41,694 --> 00:14:45,101
he stopped, as if suddenly rooted to one spot.

216
00:14:45,540 --> 00:14:47,160
He looked at me long and hard.

217
00:14:48,040 --> 00:14:51,230
I turned my eyes from him, fixed them on the fire, and

218
00:14:51,230 --> 00:14:55,199
tried to assume and maintain a quiet, collected aspect.

219
00:14:57,019 --> 00:15:01,694
Now for the hitch in Jane's character, he said at last, speaking

220
00:15:01,696 --> 00:15:05,440
more calmly than from his look I had expected him to speak.

221
00:15:06,260 --> 00:15:09,813
The reel of silk has run smoothly enough so far, but

222
00:15:09,813 --> 00:15:12,940
I always knew they would come a knot and a puzzle.

223
00:15:13,599 --> 00:15:14,599
Here it is.

224
00:15:14,959 --> 00:15:19,000
Now for vexation and exasperation and endless trouble.

225
00:15:19,680 --> 00:15:22,550
By God, I long to exert a fraction of Samson's

226
00:15:22,550 --> 00:15:25,059
strength and break the entanglement like Tau.

227
00:15:26,160 --> 00:15:31,980
He recommends his walk, but soon again stopped, and this time just before me.

228
00:15:32,639 --> 00:15:34,500
Jane, will you hear reason?

229
00:15:35,379 --> 00:15:37,940
He stooped and approached his lips to my ear.

230
00:15:38,760 --> 00:15:41,620
Because if you won't, I'll try violence.

231
00:15:42,639 --> 00:15:43,660
His voice was horse.

232
00:15:44,580 --> 00:15:47,480
His look, that of a man who is just about to burst an

233
00:15:47,482 --> 00:15:51,160
insufferable bond and plunge headlong into wild license.

234
00:15:52,199 --> 00:15:56,756
I saw that in another moment and with one impetus of

235
00:15:56,756 --> 00:15:59,921
frenzy more, I should be able to do nothing with him.

236
00:16:00,580 --> 00:16:04,186
The present, the passing second of time, was

237
00:16:04,186 --> 00:16:07,841
all I had in which to control and restrain him.

238
00:16:08,660 --> 00:16:14,319
A movement of repulsion, flight, fear would have sealed my doom and his.

239
00:16:15,559 --> 00:16:18,059
But I was not afraid, not in the least.

240
00:16:18,061 --> 00:16:20,220
I felt an inward power.

241
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,220
A sense of influence which supported me.

242
00:16:23,919 --> 00:16:29,459
The crisis was perilous, but not without its charm, such as the Indian perhaps

243
00:16:29,461 --> 00:16:32,779
feels when he slips over the rapid in his canoe.

244
00:16:33,959 --> 00:16:38,199
I took hold of his clenched hand, loosened the contorted fingers,

245
00:16:39,019 --> 00:16:44,779
and said to him soothingly, sit down, I'll talk to you as long as you like,

246
00:16:45,620 --> 00:16:50,080
and hear all you have to say, whether reasonable or unreasonable.

247
00:16:50,959 --> 00:16:55,620
He sat down, but he did not get leave to speak directly.

248
00:16:57,360 --> 00:17:00,080
I had been struggling with tears for some time.

249
00:17:00,959 --> 00:17:03,830
I had taken great pains to repress them because

250
00:17:03,832 --> 00:17:07,341
I knew he would not like to see me weep.

251
00:17:07,660 --> 00:17:13,319
Now, however, I considered it well to let them flow as freely and as long as they

252
00:17:13,321 --> 00:17:17,400
liked, if the flood annoyed him so much the better.

253
00:17:18,519 --> 00:17:21,339
So I gave way and cried heartily.

254
00:17:22,260 --> 00:17:25,680
Soon I heard him earnestly in treating me to be composed.

255
00:17:26,580 --> 00:17:31,319
I said I could not, while he was in such a passion, but I am not angry, Jane.

256
00:17:32,160 --> 00:17:37,959
I only love you too well, and you had steeled your little pale face with such a

257
00:17:37,961 --> 00:17:41,500
resolute, frozen look I could not endure it.

258
00:17:42,639 --> 00:17:44,620
Hush now and wipe your eyes.

259
00:17:45,559 --> 00:17:50,819
His softened voice announced that he was subdued, so I, in my turn, became calm.

260
00:17:51,900 --> 00:17:55,779
Now he made an effort to rest his head on my shoulder, but I would not permit it.

261
00:17:56,559 --> 00:17:58,059
Then he would draw me to him.

262
00:17:58,760 --> 00:17:59,760
No.

263
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:02,279
Jane, Jane, he said.

264
00:18:03,099 --> 00:18:07,540
In such an accent of bitter sadness, it thrilled along every nerve I had.

265
00:18:08,900 --> 00:18:09,900
You don't love me then.

266
00:18:10,720 --> 00:18:14,260
It was only my station and the rank of my wife that you valued.

267
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:19,355
Now that you think me disqualified to become your husband,

268
00:18:19,355 --> 00:18:22,879
you recoil from my touch as if I were towed or ape.

269
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,019
These words cut me.

270
00:18:27,199 --> 00:18:28,980
Yet what could I do or I say?

271
00:18:30,400 --> 00:18:35,440
I ought probably to have done or said nothing, but I was so tortured by a sense

272
00:18:35,440 --> 00:18:38,425
of remorse that thus hurting his feelings I could not

273
00:18:38,427 --> 00:18:41,021
control the wish to drop balm where I had wounded.

274
00:18:41,760 --> 00:18:44,120
I do love you, I said.

275
00:18:44,919 --> 00:18:48,180
More than ever, but I must not show or indulge the feeling.

276
00:18:49,120 --> 00:18:51,599
And this is the last time I must express it.

277
00:18:52,760 --> 00:18:54,639
The last time, Jane, what?

278
00:18:55,260 --> 00:18:57,360
Do you think you can live with me and see me daily?

279
00:18:57,940 --> 00:19:01,440
And yet, if you still love me, be always cold and distant.

280
00:19:02,660 --> 00:19:05,480
No, sir, that I am certain I could not.

281
00:19:06,199 --> 00:19:10,800
And therefore I see there is but one way, but you will be furious if I mention it.

282
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:12,580
Oh, mention it.

283
00:19:12,879 --> 00:19:15,660
If I storm, you have the art of weeping.

284
00:19:16,959 --> 00:19:19,360
Mr. Rochester, I must leave you.

285
00:19:20,000 --> 00:19:21,000
For how long, Jane?

286
00:19:21,919 --> 00:19:26,239
For a few minutes, while you smooth your hair, which is somewhat disheveled,

287
00:19:26,660 --> 00:19:30,080
and bathe your face, which looks feverish.

288
00:19:31,279 --> 00:19:33,260
I must leave Adele and Thornfield.

289
00:19:34,080 --> 00:19:36,059
I must part with you for my whole life.

290
00:19:36,980 --> 00:19:42,379
I must begin a new existence among strange faces and strange scenes.

291
00:19:43,620 --> 00:19:45,940
Of course, I told you you should.

292
00:19:46,639 --> 00:19:49,019
I pass over the madness about parting from me.

293
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:51,720
You mean you must become a part of me.

294
00:19:52,699 --> 00:19:54,879
As to the new existence, it is all right.

295
00:19:55,879 --> 00:19:57,360
You shall yet be my wife.

296
00:19:58,260 --> 00:19:59,319
I am not married.

297
00:20:00,379 --> 00:20:03,819
You shall be Mrs. Rochester, both virtually and nominally.

298
00:20:04,559 --> 00:20:07,319
I shall keep only to you so long as you and I live.

299
00:20:08,940 --> 00:20:12,000
You shall go to a place I have in the south of France.

300
00:20:12,760 --> 00:20:15,879
A white washed villa on the shores of the Mediterranean.

301
00:20:17,019 --> 00:20:21,099
There, you shall live a happy and guarded and most innocent life.

302
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:26,680
Never fear that I wish to lure you into error, to make you my mistress.

303
00:20:27,580 --> 00:20:29,000
Why did you shake your head?

304
00:20:30,059 --> 00:20:34,480
Jane, you must be reasonable, or in truth, I shall again become frantic.

305
00:20:36,279 --> 00:20:38,500
His voice and hand quivered.

306
00:20:39,080 --> 00:20:40,860
His large nostrils dilated.

307
00:20:41,059 --> 00:20:43,699
His eye blazed still, I dared to speak.

308
00:20:44,279 --> 00:20:46,379
Sir, your wife is living.

309
00:20:46,860 --> 00:20:49,459
That is a fact acknowledged this morning by yourself.

310
00:20:50,620 --> 00:20:54,459
If I lived with you as you desire, I should then be your mistress.

311
00:20:55,400 --> 00:20:57,900
To say otherwise is sophisticated, is false.

312
00:20:59,680 --> 00:21:02,379
Jane, I am not a gentle tempered man.

313
00:21:02,919 --> 00:21:03,919
You forget that.

314
00:21:04,440 --> 00:21:05,660
I am not long enduring.

315
00:21:06,459 --> 00:21:08,300
I am not cool and dispassionate.

316
00:21:08,980 --> 00:21:12,480
Out of pity to me and yourself, put your finger on my pulse.

317
00:21:13,160 --> 00:21:15,459
Feel how it throbs and beware.

318
00:21:16,400 --> 00:21:18,839
He bared his wrist and offered it to me.

319
00:21:19,779 --> 00:21:22,180
The blood was forsaking his cheek and lips.

320
00:21:23,000 --> 00:21:24,000
They were growing livid.

321
00:21:24,779 --> 00:21:26,680
I was distressed on all hands.

322
00:21:27,459 --> 00:21:32,339
To agitate him thus deeply by a resistance he so abhorred was cruel.

323
00:21:33,199 --> 00:21:35,019
To yield was out of the question.

324
00:21:35,779 --> 00:21:40,779
I did what human beings do instinctively when they are driven to utter extremity.

325
00:21:40,781 --> 00:21:43,400
Looked for aid to one higher than man.

326
00:21:44,639 --> 00:21:49,000
The words, God help me, burst involuntarily from my lips.

327
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:54,000
I am a fool, cried Mr. Rochester suddenly.

328
00:21:54,860 --> 00:21:58,260
I keep telling her I am not married and do not explain to her why.

329
00:21:59,279 --> 00:22:03,080
I forget she knows nothing of the character of that woman, or of the

330
00:22:03,080 --> 00:22:06,440
circumstances attending my infernal union with her.

331
00:22:07,040 --> 00:22:13,839
Oh, I am certain Jane will agree with me in opinion when she knows all that I know.

332
00:22:15,400 --> 00:22:20,580
Just put your hand in mind, Janet, that I may have the evidence of touch as

333
00:22:20,580 --> 00:22:24,057
well as sight to prove you are near me, and I will

334
00:22:24,057 --> 00:22:27,360
in a few words show you the real state of the case.

335
00:22:27,879 --> 00:22:29,040
Can you listen to me?

336
00:22:30,139 --> 00:22:33,980
Yes, sir, for hours, if you will, I ask only minutes.

337
00:22:34,680 --> 00:22:40,819
Jane, did you ever hear or know that I was not the eldest son of my house,

338
00:22:41,819 --> 00:22:44,120
that I had once a brother older than I?

339
00:22:45,379 --> 00:22:49,139
I remember Mrs. Fairfax told me so once, and did you

340
00:22:49,139 --> 00:22:53,500
ever hear that my father was an avaricious, grasping man.

341
00:22:54,660 --> 00:22:57,319
I have understood something to that effect.

342
00:22:58,980 --> 00:23:05,239
Well, Jane, being so, it was his resolution to keep the property together.

343
00:23:05,879 --> 00:23:10,639
He could not bear the idea of dividing his estate and leaving me a fair portion.

344
00:23:11,440 --> 00:23:16,137
All he resolved should go to my brother, Roland, yet as

345
00:23:16,139 --> 00:23:20,120
little could he endure that a son of his should be a poor man.

346
00:23:21,239 --> 00:23:23,980
I must be provided for by a wealthy marriage.

347
00:23:25,000 --> 00:23:26,480
He sought me a partner but times.

348
00:23:27,220 --> 00:23:32,319
Mr. Mason, a West India planter and merchant, was his old acquaintance.

349
00:23:33,059 --> 00:23:35,860
He was certain his possessions were real and vast.

350
00:23:36,699 --> 00:23:37,699
He made inquiries.

351
00:23:39,099 --> 00:23:41,980
Mr. Mason, he found, had a son and daughter.

352
00:23:42,620 --> 00:23:45,095
And he learned from him that he could and

353
00:23:45,097 --> 00:23:48,921
would give the latter a fortune of £30 ,000.

354
00:23:49,779 --> 00:23:50,959
That suffice.

355
00:23:52,139 --> 00:23:55,417
When I left college, I was sent out to Jamaica

356
00:23:55,419 --> 00:23:59,141
to espouse a bride already courted for me.

357
00:23:59,639 --> 00:24:03,470
My father said nothing about her money, but he told me

358
00:24:03,470 --> 00:24:07,279
Mrs. Mason was the boast of Spanish town for her beauty.

359
00:24:08,059 --> 00:24:09,239
And this was no lie.

360
00:24:10,319 --> 00:24:14,180
I found her a fine woman in the style of Blanche Ingram.

361
00:24:15,220 --> 00:24:17,099
Tall, dark and majestic.

362
00:24:17,900 --> 00:24:20,360
Her family wished to secure me because I was of a good race.

363
00:24:21,459 --> 00:24:22,459
And so did she.

364
00:24:23,459 --> 00:24:26,739
They showed her to me in parties, splendidly dressed.

365
00:24:27,519 --> 00:24:32,379
I seldom saw her alone and had very little private conversation with her.

366
00:24:33,379 --> 00:24:36,711
She flattered me and lavishly displayed for

367
00:24:36,713 --> 00:24:39,701
my pleasure, her charms and accomplishments.

368
00:24:40,279 --> 00:24:44,059
All the men in her circle seemed to admire her and envy me.

369
00:24:45,000 --> 00:24:47,480
I was dazzled, stimulated.

370
00:24:48,300 --> 00:24:51,279
My senses were excited and being ignorant,

371
00:24:51,281 --> 00:24:55,680
raw and inexperienced, I thought I loved her.

372
00:24:55,760 --> 00:25:01,559
There is no folly so besotted that the idiotic rivalries of society, the

373
00:25:01,561 --> 00:25:04,519
preroyance, the rashness, the blindness of

374
00:25:04,521 --> 00:25:08,040
youth, will not hurry a man to its commission.

375
00:25:08,419 --> 00:25:12,836
Her relatives encouraged me, competitors peaked me, she allured

376
00:25:12,838 --> 00:25:16,400
me, a marriage was achieved almost before I knew where I was.

377
00:25:17,440 --> 00:25:21,599
Oh, I have no respect for myself when I think of that act.

378
00:25:22,059 --> 00:25:25,199
An agony of inward contempt masters me.

379
00:25:25,500 --> 00:25:30,199
I never loved, I never esteemed, I did not even know her.

380
00:25:30,919 --> 00:25:34,139
I was not sure of the existence of one virtue in her nature.

381
00:25:34,900 --> 00:25:38,182
I had marked neither modesty, nor benevolence,

382
00:25:38,184 --> 00:25:41,360
nor candor, nor refinement in her mind or manners.

383
00:25:42,080 --> 00:25:46,660
And I married her, gross, groveling, mull-eyed blockhead that I was.

384
00:25:47,319 --> 00:25:48,900
With less sin I might have.

385
00:25:49,720 --> 00:25:51,839
But let me remember to whom I am speaking.

386
00:25:54,019 --> 00:25:57,900
My bride's mother I had never seen, I understood she was dead.

387
00:25:58,980 --> 00:26:01,500
The honeymoon over I learned my mistake.

388
00:26:02,459 --> 00:26:05,199
She was only mad and shut up in a lunatic asylum.

389
00:26:06,300 --> 00:26:12,860
There was a younger brother too, a complete dumb idiot, the elder one,

390
00:26:13,459 --> 00:26:18,400
whom you have seen and whom I cannot hate whilst I abhor all his kindred,

391
00:26:19,040 --> 00:26:23,760
because he has some grains of affection in his feeble mind, shown in the continued

392
00:26:23,760 --> 00:26:26,652
interest he takes in his wretched sister, and

393
00:26:26,652 --> 00:26:30,341
also in a dog-like attachment he once bore me.

394
00:26:30,839 --> 00:26:33,819
Will probably be in the same state one day.

395
00:26:35,080 --> 00:26:41,379
My father and my brother Rowland knew all this, but they thought only of the thirty

396
00:26:41,381 --> 00:26:45,480
thousand pounds, and joined in the plot against me.

397
00:26:47,099 --> 00:26:52,760
These were vile discoveries, but except for the treachery of concealment,

398
00:26:53,440 --> 00:26:56,319
I should have made them no subject of reproach to my wife.

399
00:26:57,000 --> 00:27:02,779
Even when I found her nature wholly alien to mine, her tastes obnoxious to me,

400
00:27:03,459 --> 00:27:08,919
her cast of mind common, low, narrow and singularly incapable of being led to

401
00:27:08,921 --> 00:27:12,160
anything higher, expanded to anything larger.

402
00:27:12,980 --> 00:27:18,199
When I found that I could not pass a single evening, nor even a single hour of

403
00:27:18,201 --> 00:27:23,559
the day with her in comfort, that kindly conversation could not be sustained

404
00:27:23,561 --> 00:27:28,720
between us, because whatever topic I started immediately received from her

405
00:27:28,720 --> 00:27:32,959
return at once course and trite, perverse and imbecile.

406
00:27:33,699 --> 00:27:39,779
When I perceived that I should never have a quiet or settled household, because no

407
00:27:39,781 --> 00:27:45,019
servant would bear the continued outbreaks of her violent and unreasonable temper,

408
00:27:45,459 --> 00:27:49,279
or the vexations of her absurd contradictory exacting orders,

409
00:27:50,120 --> 00:27:51,940
even then I restrained myself.

410
00:27:52,660 --> 00:27:57,959
I assured up braiding, I curtailed remonstrants, I tried to devour my

411
00:27:57,961 --> 00:28:03,019
repentance and disgust in secret, I repressed the deep antipathy I felt.

412
00:28:04,480 --> 00:28:08,622
Jane, I will not trouble you with formidable details,

413
00:28:08,622 --> 00:28:11,419
some strong words shall express what I have to say.

414
00:28:13,139 --> 00:28:16,099
I lived with that woman upstairs for years,

415
00:28:16,101 --> 00:28:19,620
and before that time she had tried me indeed.

416
00:28:20,260 --> 00:28:25,540
Her character ripened and developed with frightful rapidity, her vices sprang up

417
00:28:25,540 --> 00:28:28,855
fast and rank, they were so strong only cruelty

418
00:28:28,855 --> 00:28:32,819
could check them, and I would not use cruelty.

419
00:28:33,839 --> 00:28:39,599
What a pygmy intellect she had, and what giant propensities, how fearful

420
00:28:39,601 --> 00:28:42,260
were the curses those propensities entailed on me.

421
00:28:44,239 --> 00:28:50,839
Bertha Mason, the true daughter of an infamous mother, dragged me through all

422
00:28:50,841 --> 00:28:54,442
the hideous and degrading agonies which must attend a

423
00:28:54,444 --> 00:28:59,160
man bound to a wife at once in temperate and unchaste.

424
00:29:00,360 --> 00:29:03,523
My brother in the interval was dead, and at

425
00:29:03,525 --> 00:29:06,900
the end of the four years my father died too.

426
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:13,980
I was rich enough now, yet poor to hideous indigents, a nature the most gross,

427
00:29:14,379 --> 00:29:18,273
impure depraved I ever saw was associated with mine,

428
00:29:18,275 --> 00:29:22,580
and called by the law and by society a part of me.

429
00:29:23,819 --> 00:29:28,207
And I could not rid myself of it by any legal proceedings,

430
00:29:28,207 --> 00:29:31,400
for the doctors now discovered that my wife was mad.

431
00:29:32,260 --> 00:29:36,360
Her excesses had prematurely developed the germs of insanity.

432
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:39,220
Jane, you don't like my narrative.

433
00:29:40,019 --> 00:29:41,059
You look almost sick.

434
00:29:42,180 --> 00:29:43,779
Shall I defer the rest to another day?

435
00:29:44,940 --> 00:29:45,940
No, sir.

436
00:29:46,639 --> 00:29:47,639
Finish it now.

437
00:29:47,980 --> 00:29:48,720
I pity you.

438
00:29:48,940 --> 00:29:50,699
I do earnestly pity you.

439
00:29:52,019 --> 00:29:56,940
Pity Jane, from some people, is a noxious and insulting sort of tribute,

440
00:29:57,419 --> 00:30:01,819
which one is justified in hurling back in the teeth of those who offer it.

441
00:30:02,480 --> 00:30:06,599
But that is the sort of pity native to callous selfish hearts.

442
00:30:07,279 --> 00:30:12,152
It is a hybrid, egotistical pain at hearing of woes, crossed

443
00:30:12,152 --> 00:30:15,540
with ignorant contempt for those who have endured them.

444
00:30:16,760 --> 00:30:18,879
But that is not your pity, Jane.

445
00:30:19,959 --> 00:30:25,639
It is not the feeling of which your whole face is full at this moment, with which

446
00:30:25,641 --> 00:30:31,459
your eyes are now almost overflowing, with which your heart is heaving,

447
00:30:31,900 --> 00:30:34,360
with which your hand is trembling in mine.

448
00:30:35,319 --> 00:30:38,639
Your pity, my darling, is the suffering mother of love.

449
00:30:39,559 --> 00:30:43,059
Its anguish is the very natal pang of the divine passion.

450
00:30:43,739 --> 00:30:44,819
I accept it, Jane.

451
00:30:45,599 --> 00:30:47,480
Let the daughter have free advent.

452
00:30:48,120 --> 00:30:50,000
My arms wait to receive her.

453
00:30:51,500 --> 00:30:52,839
Now, sir, proceed.

454
00:30:53,779 --> 00:30:55,980
What did you do when you found she was mad?

455
00:30:57,339 --> 00:31:00,660
Jane, I approached the verge of despair.

456
00:31:01,779 --> 00:31:05,800
A remnant of self-respect was all that intervened between me and the Gulf.

457
00:31:06,959 --> 00:31:10,832
In the eyes of the world, I was doubtless covered with

458
00:31:10,834 --> 00:31:15,360
grimy dishonor, but I resolved to be clean in my own sight.

459
00:31:15,940 --> 00:31:21,779
And to the last, I repudiated the contamination of her crimes and wrenched

460
00:31:21,781 --> 00:31:24,319
myself from connection with her mental defects.

461
00:31:25,220 --> 00:31:29,400
Still, society associated my name and person with hers.

462
00:31:30,419 --> 00:31:35,300
I yet saw her and heard her daily, something of her breath, fuck.

463
00:31:36,040 --> 00:31:42,300
Mixed with the air I breathed, and besides, I remembered I had once been her husband.

464
00:31:42,959 --> 00:31:47,800
That recollection was then and is now inexpressibly odious to me.

465
00:31:48,680 --> 00:31:51,959
Moreover, I knew that while she lived, I could

466
00:31:51,961 --> 00:31:55,639
never be the husband of another and better wife.

467
00:31:56,519 --> 00:32:02,500
And, though five years my senior, her family and her father had lied to me

468
00:32:02,500 --> 00:32:06,919
even in the particular of her age, she was likely to live as long as I,

469
00:32:07,739 --> 00:32:11,040
being as robust in frame as she was in firm in mind.

470
00:32:11,620 --> 00:32:15,080
Thus, at the age of 26, I was hopeless.

471
00:32:16,739 --> 00:32:19,339
One night I had been awakened by her yells.

472
00:32:20,139 --> 00:32:24,400
Since the medical men had pronounced her mad, she had of course been shut up.

473
00:32:25,260 --> 00:32:28,781
It was a fiery West Indian night, one of the description

474
00:32:28,783 --> 00:32:32,059
that frequently preceded the hurricanes of those climates.

475
00:32:32,959 --> 00:32:36,900
Being unable to sleep in bed, I got up and opened the window.

476
00:32:37,980 --> 00:32:40,660
The air was like sulfur steams.

477
00:32:41,419 --> 00:32:43,540
I could find no refreshment anywhere.

478
00:32:44,739 --> 00:32:47,919
Mosquitoes came buzzing in and hummed suddenly around the room.

479
00:32:48,580 --> 00:32:53,199
The sea, which I could hear from thence, rumbled dull like an earthquake.

480
00:32:54,220 --> 00:32:56,400
Black clouds were casting up over it.

481
00:32:56,919 --> 00:33:01,220
The moon was setting in the waves, broad and red like a hot cannonball.

482
00:33:02,139 --> 00:33:08,921
She threw her last bloody glance over a world, quivering with the ferment of tempest.

483
00:33:10,220 --> 00:33:14,940
I was physically influenced by the atmosphere and seen, and my ears were

484
00:33:14,940 --> 00:33:17,940
filled with the curses the maniac still shrieked out.

485
00:33:18,980 --> 00:33:23,739
Wherein she momentarily mingled my name, with such a tone of demon hate,

486
00:33:24,279 --> 00:33:30,260
with such language, no professed harlot ever had a foul of a capillary than she.

487
00:33:31,120 --> 00:33:37,059
Though two rooms off, I heard every word, the thin partitions of the West India

488
00:33:37,061 --> 00:33:40,620
House opposing but slight obstruction to her wolfish cries.

489
00:33:41,440 --> 00:33:44,720
This life, said I at last, is hell.

490
00:33:45,419 --> 00:33:46,419
This is the air.

491
00:33:46,959 --> 00:33:48,800
Those are the sounds of the bottomless pit.

492
00:33:49,519 --> 00:33:52,080
I have a right to deliver myself from it if I can.

493
00:33:53,300 --> 00:33:56,341
The sufferings of this mortal state will leave

494
00:33:56,341 --> 00:34:00,000
me with the heavy flesh that now combers my soul.

495
00:34:00,940 --> 00:34:04,400
Of the fanatics burning eternity, I have no fear.

496
00:34:05,440 --> 00:34:09,199
There is not a future state worse than this present one.

497
00:34:09,980 --> 00:34:12,699
Let me break away and go home to God.

498
00:34:13,980 --> 00:34:17,491
I said this whilst I knelt down at an unlocked a

499
00:34:17,491 --> 00:34:20,610
trunk which contained a brace of loaded pistols.

500
00:34:21,330 --> 00:34:22,370
I meant to shoot myself.

501
00:34:23,370 --> 00:34:25,550
I only entertain the intention for a moment.

502
00:34:26,269 --> 00:34:32,690
For, not being insane, the crisis of exquisite and unalloyed despair which had

503
00:34:32,690 --> 00:34:37,809
originated the wish and design of self -destruction was passed in a second.

504
00:34:39,349 --> 00:34:46,010
A wind fresh from Europe blew over the ocean and rushed through the open casement.

505
00:34:46,050 --> 00:34:50,989
The storm broke, streamed thunder blazed and the air grew pure.

506
00:34:52,410 --> 00:34:55,330
I then framed and fixed a resolution.

507
00:34:56,750 --> 00:35:01,750
While I walked under the dripping orange trees of my wet garden and amongst its

508
00:35:05,389 --> 00:35:13,389
drenched pomegranates and pineapples, and while the refulgent dawn of the now

509
00:35:13,391 --> 00:35:17,338
-listen, for it was true wisdom that consoled me in

510
00:35:17,339 --> 00:35:20,790
that hour and showed me the right path to follow.

511
00:35:22,230 --> 00:35:28,169
The sweet wind from Europe was still whispering in the refreshed leaves and the

512
00:35:28,171 --> 00:35:31,069
Atlantic was thundering in glorious liberty.

513
00:35:32,110 --> 00:35:37,544
My heart dried up and scorched for a long time, swelled to the

514
00:35:37,544 --> 00:35:42,550
tone and filled with living blood, my being longed for renewal.

515
00:35:43,309 --> 00:35:45,230
My soul thirsted for a pure draft.

516
00:35:46,069 --> 00:35:50,290
I saw hope revive, and felt regeneration possible.

517
00:35:51,129 --> 00:35:53,677
From a flowery arch at the bottom of my garden,

518
00:35:53,677 --> 00:35:56,730
I gazed over the sea, bluer than the sky.

519
00:35:56,889 --> 00:35:58,129
The old world was beyond.

520
00:35:58,930 --> 00:36:00,629
Clear prospects opened thus.

521
00:36:01,870 --> 00:36:05,690
Go, said hope, and live again in Europe.

522
00:36:06,569 --> 00:36:09,580
There it is not known what a solid name you

523
00:36:09,580 --> 00:36:12,930
bear, nor what a filthy burden is bound to you.

524
00:36:13,730 --> 00:36:16,529
You may take the maniac with you to England, confine

525
00:36:16,531 --> 00:36:19,669
her with due attendance and precautions at Thornfield.

526
00:36:20,809 --> 00:36:26,489
Then travel yourself to what climb you will, and form what new tire you like.

527
00:36:27,489 --> 00:36:33,190
That woman, who has so abused your long suffering, so sullied your name,

528
00:36:33,449 --> 00:36:36,875
so outraged your honour, so blighted your youth,

529
00:36:36,877 --> 00:36:40,470
is not your wife, nor are you her husband.

530
00:36:41,230 --> 00:36:44,811
See that she is cared for as her condition demands, and

531
00:36:44,811 --> 00:36:48,610
you have done all that God and humanity require of you.

532
00:36:49,690 --> 00:36:54,910
Let her identity, her connection with yourself, be buried in oblivion.

533
00:36:55,589 --> 00:37:00,750
You are bound to impart them to no living being, place her in safety and comfort,

534
00:37:01,470 --> 00:37:04,589
shelter her degradation with secrecy, and leave her.

535
00:37:05,669 --> 00:37:08,550
I acted precisely on this suggestion.

536
00:37:09,629 --> 00:37:14,129
My father and brother had not made my marriage known to their acquaintance,

537
00:37:14,870 --> 00:37:21,089
because in the very first letter I wrote to a prize them of the union, having

538
00:37:21,091 --> 00:37:27,650
already begun to experience extreme disgust of its consequences, and from the

539
00:37:27,650 --> 00:37:34,489
family character and constitution seeing a hideous future opening to me, I added an

540
00:37:34,491 --> 00:37:40,790
urgent charge to keep it secret, and very soon, the infamous conduct of the

541
00:37:40,790 --> 00:37:44,483
wife my father had selected for me, was such as to

542
00:37:44,483 --> 00:37:47,809
make him blush to own her as his daughter-in-law.

543
00:37:49,010 --> 00:37:51,887
Far from desiring to publish the connection,

544
00:37:51,889 --> 00:37:55,010
he became as anxious to conceal it as myself.

545
00:37:55,970 --> 00:37:59,470
To England then, I conveyed her, a fearful

546
00:37:59,470 --> 00:38:03,031
voyage I had with such a monster in the vessel.

547
00:38:03,889 --> 00:38:09,510
Glad was I, when I had last got her to Thornfield, and saw her safely lodged in

548
00:38:09,510 --> 00:38:14,296
that third story room of whose secret in a cabinet she has

549
00:38:14,298 --> 00:38:20,150
now for ten years made a wild beast's den, a goblin cell.

550
00:38:20,150 --> 00:38:27,190
I had some trouble in finding an attendant for her, as it was necessary to select one

551
00:38:27,190 --> 00:38:30,555
on whose fidelity dependence could be placed, for

552
00:38:30,557 --> 00:38:33,930
her ravings would inevitably betray my secret.

553
00:38:34,970 --> 00:38:38,915
Besides, she had lucid intervals of days, sometimes

554
00:38:38,915 --> 00:38:42,351
weeks, which she filled up with abuse of me.

555
00:38:42,839 --> 00:38:46,269
At last, I hired Grace Paul from the Grimsey retreat.

556
00:38:47,529 --> 00:38:53,089
She and the surgeon Carter, who dressed Mason's wounds that night he was stabbed

557
00:38:53,091 --> 00:38:58,290
and worried, are the only two I have ever admitted to my confidence.

558
00:38:59,589 --> 00:39:03,678
Mrs. Fairfax may indeed have suspected something, but

559
00:39:03,680 --> 00:39:07,470
she could have gained no precise knowledge as to facts.

560
00:39:08,370 --> 00:39:15,069
Grace has, on the whole, proved a good keeper, though, owing partly to a fault of

561
00:39:15,071 --> 00:39:19,495
her own, of which it appears nothing can cure her,

562
00:39:19,495 --> 00:39:22,650
and which is incident to her harassing profession.

563
00:39:24,069 --> 00:39:27,870
Her vigilance has been more than once lulled and baffled.

564
00:39:28,690 --> 00:39:31,330
The lunatic is both cunning and malignant.

565
00:39:32,269 --> 00:39:36,470
She has never failed to take advantage of her guardian's temporary lapses,

566
00:39:37,050 --> 00:39:42,930
once to secrete the knife with which she stabbed her brother, and twice to possess

567
00:39:42,930 --> 00:39:47,370
herself of the key of her cell and issue therefrom in the night time.

568
00:39:48,209 --> 00:39:54,531
On the first of these occasions, she perpetrated the attempt to burn me in my bed.

569
00:39:54,830 --> 00:39:58,629
On the second, she paid that ghastly visit to you.

570
00:39:59,550 --> 00:40:05,209
I thank Providence, who watched over you, that she then spent her fury on your

571
00:40:05,211 --> 00:40:07,709
wedding apparel, which perhaps brought back

572
00:40:07,711 --> 00:40:11,370
vague reminiscences of her own bridal days.

573
00:40:11,430 --> 00:40:15,930
But on what might have happened, I cannot endure to reflect.

574
00:40:16,629 --> 00:40:21,790
When I think of the thing which flew at my throat this morning, hanging its black and

575
00:40:21,790 --> 00:40:26,150
scarlet visage over the nest of my dove, my blood curdles.

576
00:40:27,349 --> 00:40:33,709
And what, sir, I asked, while he paused, did you do when you had settled her here?

577
00:40:33,989 --> 00:40:34,989
Where did you go?

578
00:40:35,790 --> 00:40:37,029
What did I do, Jane?

579
00:40:37,849 --> 00:40:40,230
I transformed myself into a will of the wisp.

580
00:40:40,709 --> 00:40:41,709
Where did I go?

581
00:40:42,709 --> 00:40:46,709
I pursued wanderings as wild as those of the march spirit.

582
00:40:46,711 --> 00:40:51,930
I sought the continent, and went devious through all its lands.

583
00:40:53,169 --> 00:40:58,389
My fixed desire was to seek and find a good and intelligent woman whom I could

584
00:40:58,391 --> 00:41:02,129
love, a contrast to the fury I left at Thornfield.

585
00:41:02,930 --> 00:41:04,750
But you could not marry, sir.

586
00:41:05,790 --> 00:41:09,470
I had determined and was convinced that I could and ought.

587
00:41:10,330 --> 00:41:15,410
It was not my original intention to deceive, as I have deceived you.

588
00:41:16,709 --> 00:41:22,370
I meant to tell my tale plainly, and make my proposals openly, and it

589
00:41:22,370 --> 00:41:25,139
appeared to me so absolutely rational that I

590
00:41:25,139 --> 00:41:29,110
should be considered free to love and be loved.

591
00:41:29,470 --> 00:41:34,389
I never doubted some woman might be found willing and able to understand my case and

592
00:41:34,391 --> 00:41:39,510
accept me, in spite of the curse with which I was burdened.

593
00:41:39,910 --> 00:41:40,910
Well, sir?

594
00:41:42,010 --> 00:41:46,410
When you are inquisitive, Jane, you always make me smile.

595
00:41:47,669 --> 00:41:52,529
You open your eyes like an eager bird, and make every now and then a restless

596
00:41:52,531 --> 00:41:56,923
movement, as if answers in speech did not flow fast enough

597
00:41:56,923 --> 00:42:00,629
for you, and you wanted to read the tablet of one's heart.

598
00:42:01,550 --> 00:42:05,870
But before I go on, tell me what you mean by your... well, sir.

599
00:42:07,349 --> 00:42:11,368
It is a small phrase, very frequent with you, and which many

600
00:42:11,368 --> 00:42:14,849
a time has drawn me on and on through interminable talk.

601
00:42:15,669 --> 00:42:16,870
I don't very well know why.

602
00:42:17,989 --> 00:42:19,330
I mean, what next?

603
00:42:20,089 --> 00:42:20,769
How did you proceed?

604
00:42:20,949 --> 00:42:22,589
What came of such an event?

605
00:42:23,830 --> 00:42:24,830
Precisely.

606
00:42:25,230 --> 00:42:26,910
And what do you wish to know now?

607
00:42:28,110 --> 00:42:32,690
Whether you found anyone you liked, whether you asked her to marry you,

608
00:42:33,110 --> 00:42:34,110
and what she said.

609
00:42:35,129 --> 00:42:40,531
I can tell you whether I found anyone I liked, and whether I asked her to marry me.

610
00:42:40,629 --> 00:42:43,949
But what she said is yet to be recorded in the book of Fate.

611
00:42:45,190 --> 00:42:51,730
For ten long years I roved about, living first in one capital, then another.

612
00:42:52,470 --> 00:42:56,044
Sometimes in St. Petersburg, often in Paris,

613
00:42:56,046 --> 00:42:59,790
occasionally in Rome, Naples and Florence.

614
00:43:00,730 --> 00:43:03,572
Provided with plenty of money and the passport

615
00:43:03,574 --> 00:43:06,750
of an old name, I could choose my own society.

616
00:43:07,430 --> 00:43:09,349
No circles were closed against me.

617
00:43:10,569 --> 00:43:15,449
I sought my ideal of a woman amongst English ladies, French contesses,

618
00:43:15,930 --> 00:43:18,930
Italian seniors, and German graffinians.

619
00:43:19,709 --> 00:43:21,510
I could not find her.

620
00:43:22,489 --> 00:43:27,290
Sometimes, for a fleeting moment, I thought I caught a glance, heard a tone,

621
00:43:27,669 --> 00:43:30,930
beheld a form, which announced the realization

622
00:43:30,932 --> 00:43:33,569
of my dream, but I was presently underseafed.

623
00:43:34,489 --> 00:43:39,669
You are not to suppose that I desired perfection, either of mind or person.

624
00:43:40,269 --> 00:43:44,589
I longed only for what suited me, for the antipodes of the Creole,

625
00:43:45,129 --> 00:43:46,489
and I longed vainly.

626
00:43:46,910 --> 00:43:51,610
Amongst them all, I found not one whom had I been ever so free.

627
00:43:52,129 --> 00:43:55,633
I warned as I was of the risks, the horrors, the low

628
00:43:55,633 --> 00:43:59,650
things of incongruous unions would have asked to marry me.

629
00:44:00,489 --> 00:44:01,989
Disappointment made me reckless.

630
00:44:02,709 --> 00:44:05,010
I tried dissipation, never debauchery.

631
00:44:05,569 --> 00:44:07,709
That I hated and hate.

632
00:44:08,669 --> 00:44:12,504
That was my Indian messelina's attribute, rooted disgust

633
00:44:12,504 --> 00:44:16,309
at it, and her restrained me much, even in pleasure.

634
00:44:17,230 --> 00:44:22,050
Any enjoyment that bordered on riot seemed to approach me to her and her vices,

635
00:44:22,889 --> 00:44:23,889
and I issued it.

636
00:44:24,889 --> 00:44:29,389
Yet I could not live alone, so I tried the companionship of mistresses.

637
00:44:30,190 --> 00:44:34,963
The first I chose was Celine Varense, another of those

638
00:44:34,963 --> 00:44:38,849
steps which make a man spurn himself when he recalls them.

639
00:44:40,050 --> 00:44:44,370
You already know what she was and how my liaison with her terminated.

640
00:44:45,250 --> 00:44:50,065
She had two successes, an Italian, Jacinta and a

641
00:44:50,067 --> 00:44:53,449
German, Clara, both considered singularly handsome.

642
00:44:54,330 --> 00:44:56,949
What was their beauty to me in a few weeks?

643
00:44:57,889 --> 00:45:00,430
Jacinta was unprincipled and violent.

644
00:45:01,309 --> 00:45:02,889
I tired of her in three months.

645
00:45:03,949 --> 00:45:07,576
Clara was honest and quiet, but heavy, mindless

646
00:45:07,578 --> 00:45:11,290
and unimpressable, not one wit to my taste.

647
00:45:11,529 --> 00:45:15,449
I was glad to give her a sufficient sum to set her up in a good line of business,

648
00:45:15,989 --> 00:45:17,269
and so get decently rid of her.

649
00:45:18,830 --> 00:45:22,091
But Jane, I see by your face, you are not

650
00:45:22,093 --> 00:45:26,370
forming a very favourable opinion of me just now.

651
00:45:26,569 --> 00:45:30,449
You think me an unfeeling loose, principled rake, don't you?

652
00:45:31,889 --> 00:45:36,029
I don't like you so well as I have done sometimes, indeed, sir.

653
00:45:37,029 --> 00:45:40,209
Did it not seem to you in the least wrong to live in that way?

654
00:45:41,010 --> 00:45:43,550
First with one mistress, and then another?

655
00:45:44,370 --> 00:45:46,309
You talk of it as a mere matter of course.

656
00:45:48,190 --> 00:45:50,690
It was with me, and I did not like it.

657
00:45:51,470 --> 00:45:53,629
It was a groveling fashion of existence.

658
00:45:54,629 --> 00:45:56,430
I should never like to return to it.

659
00:45:57,730 --> 00:46:01,610
Hiring a mistress is the next worst thing to buying a slave.

660
00:46:02,330 --> 00:46:06,569
Both are often by nature and always by position, inferior.

661
00:46:07,510 --> 00:46:10,629
And to live familiarly with inferior is degrading.

662
00:46:11,529 --> 00:46:17,610
I now hate the recollection of the time I passed with Saline, Jacinta, and Clara.

663
00:46:19,510 --> 00:46:25,569
I felt the truth of these words, and I drew from them the certain inference

664
00:46:25,571 --> 00:46:31,370
that if I was so far to forget myself and all the teaching that had ever been

665
00:46:31,370 --> 00:46:37,750
instilled into me as under any pretext, with any justification, through any

666
00:46:37,750 --> 00:46:41,809
temptation, to become the successor of these poor girls.

667
00:46:42,589 --> 00:46:47,230
He would one day regard me with the same feeling, which now in his mind,

668
00:46:47,790 --> 00:46:49,129
desecrated their memory.

669
00:46:50,209 --> 00:46:52,430
I did not give utterance to this conviction.

670
00:46:53,169 --> 00:46:54,669
It was enough to feel it.

671
00:46:55,389 --> 00:46:58,142
I impressed it on my heart that it might remain

672
00:46:58,144 --> 00:47:01,050
there to serve me as aid in the time of trial.

673
00:47:01,849 --> 00:47:05,730
Now, Jane, why don't you say, well sir?

674
00:47:06,550 --> 00:47:07,569
I have not done.

675
00:47:08,010 --> 00:47:09,010
You are looking grave.

676
00:47:09,650 --> 00:47:11,550
You disapprove of me still, I see.

677
00:47:12,290 --> 00:47:13,650
But let me come to the point.

678
00:47:14,849 --> 00:47:20,389
Last January, rid of all mistresses, in a harsh, bitter frame of mind,

679
00:47:21,050 --> 00:47:26,690
the result of a useless, roving, lonely life, corroded with disappointment,

680
00:47:27,389 --> 00:47:32,510
sourly disposed against all men, and especially against all woman kind.

681
00:47:33,089 --> 00:47:36,773
For I began to regard the notion of an intellectual,

682
00:47:36,773 --> 00:47:39,790
faithful, loving woman as a mere dream.

683
00:47:41,110 --> 00:47:44,269
Recalled by business, I came back to England.

684
00:47:45,870 --> 00:47:50,569
On a frosty winter afternoon, I rode in sight of Thornfield Hall.

685
00:47:51,489 --> 00:47:56,769
A poor at spot, I expected no peace, no pleasure there.

686
00:47:58,150 --> 00:48:02,190
On a style in a lane, I saw a quiet little figure sitting by itself.

687
00:48:03,190 --> 00:48:06,949
I passed it as negligently as I did the Pollard Willow opposite to it.

688
00:48:07,910 --> 00:48:10,750
I had no presentiment of what it would be to me.

689
00:48:11,529 --> 00:48:17,389
No inward warning that the arbitress of my life, my genius for good or evil,

690
00:48:18,069 --> 00:48:20,010
waited there in humble guise.

691
00:48:20,690 --> 00:48:21,769
I did not know it.

692
00:48:22,330 --> 00:48:25,110
Even when, on the occasion of measure was

693
00:48:25,112 --> 00:48:29,150
accident, it came up and gravely offered me help.

694
00:48:29,790 --> 00:48:31,790
Childish and slender creature.

695
00:48:32,769 --> 00:48:35,493
It seemed as if a limit had hopped to my foot

696
00:48:35,493 --> 00:48:39,071
and proposed to bear me on its tiny wing.

697
00:48:39,309 --> 00:48:42,650
I was surly, but the thing would not go.

698
00:48:43,349 --> 00:48:46,105
It stood by me with strange perseverance and

699
00:48:46,105 --> 00:48:49,250
looked and spoke with a sort of authority.

700
00:48:49,769 --> 00:48:53,610
I must be aided and by that hand and aided I was.

701
00:48:54,569 --> 00:48:58,822
When once I had pressed the frail shoulder, something

702
00:48:58,822 --> 00:49:02,769
new, a fresh sap and sense stole into my frame.

703
00:49:03,930 --> 00:49:09,029
It was well I had learnt that this elf must return to me, that it belonged to my

704
00:49:09,031 --> 00:49:15,449
house down below, or I could not have felt it pass away from under my hand and seen

705
00:49:15,451 --> 00:49:19,629
it vanish behind the dim hedge without singular regret.

706
00:49:21,110 --> 00:49:24,866
I heard you come home that night, Jane, though probably you

707
00:49:24,868 --> 00:49:28,309
were not aware that I thought of you or watched for you.

708
00:49:29,569 --> 00:49:34,338
The next day I observed you, myself unseen, for half

709
00:49:34,338 --> 00:49:37,610
an hour, while you played with Adele in the gallery.

710
00:49:38,370 --> 00:49:43,230
It was a snowy day, I recollect, and you could not go out of doors.

711
00:49:44,150 --> 00:49:45,150
I was in my room.

712
00:49:45,949 --> 00:49:46,949
The door was a jar.

713
00:49:47,650 --> 00:49:49,709
I could both listen and watch.

714
00:49:50,669 --> 00:49:53,809
Adele claimed your outward attention for a while,

715
00:49:53,811 --> 00:49:57,050
yet I fancied your thoughts were elsewhere.

716
00:49:57,449 --> 00:50:00,169
But you were very patient with her, my little Jane.

717
00:50:01,209 --> 00:50:03,650
You talked to her and amused her a long time.

718
00:50:04,769 --> 00:50:09,750
When at last she left you, you lapsed at once into deep reverie.

719
00:50:10,470 --> 00:50:13,290
You betook yourself slowly to pace the gallery.

720
00:50:14,110 --> 00:50:20,250
Now and then, in passing a casement, you glanced out at the thick, falling snow.

721
00:50:20,690 --> 00:50:26,690
You listened to the sobbing wind, and again, you paced gently on and dreamed.

722
00:50:27,849 --> 00:50:30,269
I think those day visions were not dark.

723
00:50:31,510 --> 00:50:34,430
There was a pleasurable illumination in your eye occasionally.

724
00:50:35,410 --> 00:50:40,250
A soft excitement in your aspect, which told of no bitter, billious,

725
00:50:40,489 --> 00:50:41,809
hyperchondriac brooding.

726
00:50:42,449 --> 00:50:46,970
Your look revealed rather the sweet musings of youth, when its spirit follows

727
00:50:46,970 --> 00:50:51,690
on willing wings the flight of hope up and on to an ideal heaven.

728
00:50:52,470 --> 00:50:57,769
The voice of Mrs Fairfax, speaking to a servant in the hall, wakened you.

729
00:50:58,889 --> 00:51:03,110
And how curiously you smiled to and at yourself, Janet.

730
00:51:03,830 --> 00:51:05,949
There was much sense in your smile.

731
00:51:06,750 --> 00:51:10,949
It was very shrewd and seemed to make light of your own abstraction.

732
00:51:11,550 --> 00:51:15,836
It seemed to say, my fine visions are all very well,

733
00:51:15,838 --> 00:51:19,569
but I must not forget they are absolutely unreal.

734
00:51:20,529 --> 00:51:26,410
I have a rosy sky and a green flowery Eden in my brain, but without, I am perfectly

735
00:51:26,411 --> 00:51:30,203
aware, lies at my feet, a rough tract to travel,

736
00:51:30,203 --> 00:51:33,989
and around me gather black tempests to encounter.

737
00:51:35,349 --> 00:51:39,690
You ran downstairs and demanded of Mrs Fairfax some occupation.

738
00:51:40,330 --> 00:51:45,449
The weekly house accounts to make up, or something of that sort, I think it was.

739
00:51:45,830 --> 00:51:49,050
I was vexed with you for getting out of my sight.

740
00:51:50,849 --> 00:51:56,029
Impatiently, I waited for evening when I might summon you to my presence.

741
00:51:56,970 --> 00:52:02,769
An unusual, to me, a perfectly new character I suspected was yours.

742
00:52:03,470 --> 00:52:06,150
I desired to search it deeper and know it better.

743
00:52:06,769 --> 00:52:11,190
You entered the room with a look and air at once shy and independent.

744
00:52:12,069 --> 00:52:13,410
You were quaintly dressed?

745
00:52:14,169 --> 00:52:15,169
Much as you are now.

746
00:52:15,989 --> 00:52:16,989
I made you talk.

747
00:52:18,010 --> 00:52:21,069
Air long, I found you full of strange contrasts.

748
00:52:21,790 --> 00:52:24,110
Your garb and manner were restricted by rule.

749
00:52:24,949 --> 00:52:29,569
Your air was often diffident, and altogether that of one refined by nature,

750
00:52:30,250 --> 00:52:32,589
but absolutely unused to society.

751
00:52:33,470 --> 00:52:36,180
And a good deal afraid of making herself

752
00:52:36,180 --> 00:52:39,970
disadvantageously conspicuous by some solicism or blunder.

753
00:52:40,809 --> 00:52:44,754
Yet when addressed, you lifted a keen, a daring,

754
00:52:44,754 --> 00:52:47,730
and a glowing eye to your interlock you to face.

755
00:52:48,910 --> 00:52:52,470
There was penetration and power in each glance you gave.

756
00:52:53,449 --> 00:52:58,730
When plied by close questions, you found ready and round answers.

757
00:53:00,230 --> 00:53:02,269
Very soon you seemed to get used to me.

758
00:53:03,050 --> 00:53:05,741
I believe you felt the existence of sympathy

759
00:53:05,741 --> 00:53:08,970
between you and your grim and crossmaster, Jane.

760
00:53:10,069 --> 00:53:12,879
For it was astonishing to see how quickly a

761
00:53:12,881 --> 00:53:16,811
certain pleasant ease tranquilized your manner.

762
00:53:17,089 --> 00:53:18,410
Snarl as I would.

763
00:53:19,169 --> 00:53:23,629
You showed no surprise, fear, annoyance, or displeasure at my moroceness.

764
00:53:24,569 --> 00:53:27,930
You watched me, and now, and then smiled at me with

765
00:53:27,932 --> 00:53:30,891
a simple yet sagacious grace I cannot describe.

766
00:53:31,419 --> 00:53:34,489
I was at once content and stimulated with what I saw.

767
00:53:35,230 --> 00:53:38,510
I liked what I had seen and wished to see more.

768
00:53:39,330 --> 00:53:45,889
Yet, for a long time, I treated you distantly and sought your company rarely.

769
00:53:46,470 --> 00:53:49,921
I was an intellectual epicure and wished to prolong the

770
00:53:49,921 --> 00:53:53,730
gratification of making this novel and peacant acquaintance.

771
00:53:54,430 --> 00:53:58,455
Besides, I was for a while troubled with a haunting fear

772
00:53:58,455 --> 00:54:02,809
that if I handled the flower freely, its bloom would fade.

773
00:54:03,769 --> 00:54:06,110
The sweet charm of freshness would leave it.

774
00:54:06,930 --> 00:54:12,389
I did not then know that it was no transitory blossom, but rather the radiant

775
00:54:12,391 --> 00:54:16,230
resemblance of one, cut in an indestructible gem.

776
00:54:17,830 --> 00:54:20,580
Moreover, I wished to see whether you would

777
00:54:20,582 --> 00:54:23,550
seek me if I shunned you, but you did not.

778
00:54:24,410 --> 00:54:27,529
You kept in the school room as still as your own desk and easel.

779
00:54:28,250 --> 00:54:33,910
If by chance I met you, you passed me as soon, and with as little token of

780
00:54:33,911 --> 00:54:36,849
recognition, as was consistent with respect.

781
00:54:38,110 --> 00:54:44,150
Your habitual expression in those days, Jane, was a thoughtful look, not despondent.

782
00:54:44,589 --> 00:54:47,796
For you were not sickly, but not buoyant, for

783
00:54:47,796 --> 00:54:51,351
you had little hope and no actual pleasure.

784
00:54:52,209 --> 00:54:55,625
I wondered what you thought of me, or if you ever

785
00:54:55,627 --> 00:54:58,669
thought of me, and resolved to find this out.

786
00:54:59,750 --> 00:55:01,870
I resumed my notice of you.

787
00:55:02,650 --> 00:55:08,050
There was something glad in your glance and genial in your manner when you conversed.

788
00:55:08,370 --> 00:55:10,330
I saw you had a social heart.

789
00:55:10,989 --> 00:55:12,569
It was the silent school room.

790
00:55:13,190 --> 00:55:15,989
It was the tedium of your life that made you mournful.

791
00:55:16,870 --> 00:55:19,970
I permitted myself the delight of being kind to you.

792
00:55:20,690 --> 00:55:23,110
Kindness stirred emotion soon.

793
00:55:24,169 --> 00:55:26,209
Your face became soft in expression.

794
00:55:26,870 --> 00:55:27,989
Your tone's gentle.

795
00:55:29,069 --> 00:55:33,650
I liked my name pronounced by your lips in a grateful, happy accent.

796
00:55:35,029 --> 00:55:38,870
I used to enjoy a chance meeting with you, Jane, at this time.

797
00:55:39,569 --> 00:55:42,169
There was a curious hesitation in your manner.

798
00:55:43,069 --> 00:55:47,110
You glanced at me with a slight trouble, a hovering doubt.

799
00:55:48,129 --> 00:55:51,843
You did not know what my caprice might be, whether I was going

800
00:55:51,845 --> 00:55:57,069
to play the master and be stern, or the friend and be benignant.

801
00:55:57,970 --> 00:56:02,089
I was now too fond of you often to simulate the first whim.

802
00:56:02,989 --> 00:56:06,822
And when I stretched my hand out cordially, such bloom

803
00:56:06,822 --> 00:56:10,610
and light and bliss rose to your young, wistful features.

804
00:56:11,349 --> 00:56:16,410
I had much ado often to avoid straining you then and there to my heart.

805
00:56:17,910 --> 00:56:20,250
Don't talk anymore of those days, sir.

806
00:56:21,029 --> 00:56:22,029
I interrupted.

807
00:56:22,470 --> 00:56:25,510
Fertively dashing away some tears from my eyes.

808
00:56:26,010 --> 00:56:27,989
His language was torture to me.

809
00:56:28,589 --> 00:56:31,010
For I knew what I must do and do soon.

810
00:56:31,629 --> 00:56:34,544
And all these reminiscences and these revelations

811
00:56:34,544 --> 00:56:37,169
of his feelings only made my work more difficult.

812
00:56:38,209 --> 00:56:40,029
No, Jane, he returned.

813
00:56:40,809 --> 00:56:42,910
What necessity is there to dwell on the past?

814
00:56:43,529 --> 00:56:48,029
When the present is so much sure, the future so much brighter.

815
00:56:49,430 --> 00:56:51,849
I shuddered to hear the infatuated assertion.

816
00:56:52,910 --> 00:56:55,029
You see now how the case stands.

817
00:56:55,349 --> 00:56:55,830
Do you not?

818
00:56:56,370 --> 00:56:57,370
He continued.

819
00:56:57,889 --> 00:57:00,413
After a youth in manhood passed half in

820
00:57:00,413 --> 00:57:04,091
unalterable misery and half in dreary solitude.

821
00:57:04,470 --> 00:57:08,430
I have, for the first time, found what I can truly love.

822
00:57:09,349 --> 00:57:10,410
I have found you.

823
00:57:11,069 --> 00:57:15,069
You are my sympathy, my better self, my good angel.

824
00:57:15,870 --> 00:57:18,129
I am bound to you with a strong attachment.

825
00:57:19,069 --> 00:57:21,410
I think you good, gifted, lovely.

826
00:57:22,190 --> 00:57:25,330
A fervent, a solemn passion is conceived in my heart.

827
00:57:26,089 --> 00:57:31,669
It leans to you, draws you to my center and spring of life, wraps my existence

828
00:57:31,671 --> 00:57:38,129
about you, and kindling in pure, powerful flame fuses you and me in one.

829
00:57:39,669 --> 00:57:45,589
It was because I felt and knew this that I resolved to marry you.

830
00:57:46,230 --> 00:57:49,529
To tell me that I had already a wife is empty mockery.

831
00:57:50,230 --> 00:57:52,849
You know now that I had but a hideous demon.

832
00:57:53,709 --> 00:57:55,809
I was wrong to attempt to deceive you.

833
00:57:56,769 --> 00:58:00,209
But I feared a stubbornness that exists in your character.

834
00:58:01,449 --> 00:58:03,889
I feared early instilled prejudice.

835
00:58:04,709 --> 00:58:07,769
I wanted to have you safe before hazarding confidences.

836
00:58:08,610 --> 00:58:10,389
This was cowardly.

837
00:58:11,010 --> 00:58:15,750
I should have appealed to your nobleness and magnanimity at first, as I do now,

838
00:58:16,430 --> 00:58:19,150
open to you plainly, my life of agony.

839
00:58:20,069 --> 00:58:23,870
Describe to you my hunger and thirst after a higher and worthyer existence,

840
00:58:24,750 --> 00:58:31,129
shown to you not my resolution that word is weak, but my resisteless bent to love

841
00:58:31,131 --> 00:58:36,029
faithfully and well, where I am faithfully and well loved in return.

842
00:58:37,089 --> 00:58:40,690
Then I should have asked you to accept my pleasure fidelity and to give me yours.

843
00:58:41,370 --> 00:58:44,629
Jane, give it me now, a pause.

844
00:58:45,650 --> 00:58:47,269
Why are you silent, Jane?

845
00:58:47,271 --> 00:58:50,370
I was experiencing an ordeal.

846
00:58:51,150 --> 00:58:56,569
A hand of fiery iron grasped my vitals, terrible moment, full of struggle,

847
00:58:56,889 --> 00:58:59,616
blackness, burning, not a human being that ever

848
00:58:59,618 --> 00:59:02,989
lived could wish to be loved better than I was loved.

849
00:59:03,510 --> 00:59:06,815
And him, who thus loved me, I absolutely

850
00:59:06,815 --> 00:59:11,571
worshipped, and I must renounce love and idol.

851
00:59:12,309 --> 00:59:14,830
One drear word comprised my intolerable duty.

852
00:59:15,449 --> 00:59:16,449
Depart!

853
00:59:17,150 --> 00:59:19,250
Jane, you understand what I want of you?

854
00:59:19,709 --> 00:59:22,269
Just this promise, I will be yours, Mr. Rochester.

855
00:59:23,129 --> 00:59:25,250
Mr. Rochester, I will not be yours.

856
00:59:26,349 --> 00:59:27,349
Another long silence.

857
00:59:28,529 --> 00:59:33,150
Jane, recommenced he, with a gentleness that broke me down with grief,

858
00:59:33,970 --> 00:59:36,773
and turned me stone-cold with ominous terror for

859
00:59:36,773 --> 00:59:39,910
this still voice was the pant of a lion rising.

860
00:59:41,410 --> 00:59:45,669
Jane, do you mean to go one way in the world and to let me go another?

861
00:59:46,730 --> 00:59:47,730
I do.

862
00:59:48,430 --> 00:59:51,010
Jane, bending towards and embracing me.

863
00:59:51,410 --> 00:59:52,410
Do you mean it now?

864
00:59:52,889 --> 00:59:53,169
I do.

865
00:59:53,830 --> 00:59:59,129
And now, softly kissing my forehead and cheek, I do,

866
00:59:59,129 --> 01:00:02,809
extricating myself from restraint rapidly and completely.

867
01:00:03,489 --> 01:00:08,050
Oh, Jane, this is bitter, this, this is wicked, it would not be wicked to love me.

868
01:00:08,489 --> 01:00:14,250
It would to obey you, a wild look raised his brows, crossed his features,

869
01:00:14,769 --> 01:00:17,050
he rose, but he forebore yet.

870
01:00:18,269 --> 01:00:23,930
I laid my hand on the back of a chair for support, I shook, I feared, but I resolved.

871
01:00:24,870 --> 01:00:30,529
One instant, Jane, give one glance to my horrible life when you are gone.

872
01:00:31,510 --> 01:00:33,470
All happiness will be torn away with you.

873
01:00:34,430 --> 01:00:35,430
What then is left.

874
01:00:36,730 --> 01:00:40,341
For a wife, I have but the maniac upstairs, as well

875
01:00:40,343 --> 01:00:43,349
might you refer me to some corpse in Yonder Churchyard.

876
01:00:44,349 --> 01:00:45,730
What shall I do, Jane?

877
01:00:46,809 --> 01:00:49,069
We're turned for a companion and for some hope.

878
01:00:50,089 --> 01:00:54,569
Do as I do, trusting God and yourself, believe in heaven.

879
01:00:55,449 --> 01:00:56,489
Hope to meet again there.

880
01:00:57,550 --> 01:00:58,550
Then you will not yield?

881
01:00:59,470 --> 01:01:00,470
No.

882
01:01:00,830 --> 01:01:04,110
Then you condemn me to live wretched and to die a curse.

883
01:01:04,510 --> 01:01:05,849
His voice rose.

884
01:01:06,690 --> 01:01:10,930
I advise you to live sinless and I wish you to die tranquil.

885
01:01:12,449 --> 01:01:14,910
Then you snatch love and innocence from me.

886
01:01:15,489 --> 01:01:18,790
You fling me back on lust for a passion, vice for an occupation?

887
01:01:20,529 --> 01:01:25,610
Mr. Rochester, I know more assign this fate to you than I grasp at it for myself.

888
01:01:26,510 --> 01:01:28,489
We were born to strive and endure.

889
01:01:29,510 --> 01:01:31,069
You as well as I do so.

890
01:01:31,830 --> 01:01:34,370
You will forget me before I forget you.

891
01:01:35,989 --> 01:01:38,069
You make me a liar by such language.

892
01:01:38,970 --> 01:01:40,129
You sully my honour.

893
01:01:40,949 --> 01:01:42,470
I declared I could not change.

894
01:01:42,910 --> 01:01:45,230
You tell me to my face I shall change soon.

895
01:01:46,069 --> 01:01:49,569
And what a distortion in your judgment, what a

896
01:01:49,569 --> 01:01:53,031
perversity in your ideas is proved by your conduct.

897
01:01:53,930 --> 01:01:56,552
Is it better to drive a fellow creature to

898
01:01:56,552 --> 01:02:00,571
despair than to transgress a mere human law?

899
01:02:00,730 --> 01:02:02,849
No man being injured by the breach.

900
01:02:03,809 --> 01:02:06,743
For you have neither relatives nor acquaintances

901
01:02:06,743 --> 01:02:10,190
whom you need fear to offend by living with me.

902
01:02:11,089 --> 01:02:12,410
This was true.

903
01:02:13,089 --> 01:02:18,309
And while he spoke my very conscience and reason, turned traitors against me,

904
01:02:18,769 --> 01:02:23,989
and charged me with crime in resisting him, they spoke almost as loud as feeling,

905
01:02:24,589 --> 01:02:26,010
and that clamoured wildly.

906
01:02:26,790 --> 01:02:28,489
Oh, comply, it said.

907
01:02:29,169 --> 01:02:30,169
Think of his misery.

908
01:02:30,790 --> 01:02:31,790
Think of his danger.

909
01:02:32,669 --> 01:02:34,489
Look at his state when left alone.

910
01:02:35,209 --> 01:02:36,830
Remember his headlong nature.

911
01:02:37,629 --> 01:02:40,550
Consider the recklessness following on despair.

912
01:02:41,470 --> 01:02:46,430
Sooth him, save him, love him, tell him you love him and will be his.

913
01:02:47,150 --> 01:02:49,209
Who in the world cares for you?

914
01:02:49,809 --> 01:02:51,550
Or who will be injured by what you do?

915
01:02:52,550 --> 01:02:54,330
Still indomitable was the reply.

916
01:02:55,110 --> 01:02:56,250
I care for myself.

917
01:02:57,389 --> 01:03:03,110
The more solitary, the more friendless, the more unsastained I am, the more I will

918
01:03:03,110 --> 01:03:08,470
respect myself, I will keep the law given by God, sanctioned by man.

919
01:03:09,610 --> 01:03:12,273
I will hold to the principles received by

920
01:03:12,273 --> 01:03:16,391
me when I was sane, and not mad as I am now.

921
01:03:16,849 --> 01:03:21,470
Laws and principles are not for the times when there is no temptation.

922
01:03:22,309 --> 01:03:25,357
They are for such moments as this, when body

923
01:03:25,358 --> 01:03:28,591
and soul rise in mutiny against their rigor.

924
01:03:28,910 --> 01:03:31,989
Strangent are they, in violet they shall be.

925
01:03:33,230 --> 01:03:38,129
If at my individual convenience I might break them, what would be their worth?

926
01:03:39,389 --> 01:03:44,790
They have a worth, so I have always believed, and if I cannot believe it now,

927
01:03:45,709 --> 01:03:52,629
it is because I am insane, quite insane, with my veins running fire and my heart

928
01:03:52,631 --> 01:03:55,110
beating faster than I can count its throbs.

929
01:03:56,269 --> 01:03:59,722
Preconceived opinions, foregone determinations,

930
01:03:59,724 --> 01:04:02,489
are all I have at this hour to stand by.

931
01:04:03,169 --> 01:04:05,050
There I plant my foot.

932
01:04:06,510 --> 01:04:07,510
I did.

933
01:04:08,569 --> 01:04:12,430
Mr. Rochester, reading my countenance saw I had done so.

934
01:04:13,190 --> 01:04:15,629
His fury was wrought to the highest.

935
01:04:16,430 --> 01:04:19,290
He must yield to it for a moment whatever followed.

936
01:04:19,970 --> 01:04:23,790
He crossed the floor and seized my arm and grasped my waist.

937
01:04:24,489 --> 01:04:27,169
He seemed to devour me with his flaming glance.

938
01:04:28,190 --> 01:04:31,377
Physically I felt, at the moment, powerless as

939
01:04:31,379 --> 01:04:34,389
stubble exposed to the draught and glow of a furnace.

940
01:04:35,370 --> 01:04:42,150
Mentally, I still possessed my soul, and with it, the certainty of ultimate safety.

941
01:04:42,730 --> 01:04:45,610
The soul, fortunately, has an interpreter.

942
01:04:46,309 --> 01:04:49,650
Often an unconscious, but still a truthful interpreter in the eye.

943
01:04:50,709 --> 01:04:52,290
My eye rose to his.

944
01:04:53,290 --> 01:04:56,589
And while I looked in his fierce face, I gave an involuntary sigh.

945
01:04:57,349 --> 01:05:02,250
His gripe was painful, and my overtaxed strength almost exhausted.

946
01:05:03,930 --> 01:05:07,150
Never said he, as he ground his teeth.

947
01:05:07,870 --> 01:05:11,830
Never was anything at once so frail and so indomitable.

948
01:05:12,569 --> 01:05:15,050
A mere read she feels in my hand.

949
01:05:15,930 --> 01:05:18,129
And he shook me with the force of his hold.

950
01:05:19,129 --> 01:05:20,949
I could bend her with my finger and thumb.

951
01:05:21,709 --> 01:05:26,709
And what good would it do if I bent, if I up tore, if I crushed her?

952
01:05:27,629 --> 01:05:28,870
Consider that eye.

953
01:05:29,569 --> 01:05:33,902
Consider the resolute wild, free thing looking out of it,

954
01:05:33,904 --> 01:05:38,150
defying me with more than courage, with a stern triumph.

955
01:05:39,110 --> 01:05:41,730
Whatever I do with its cage, I cannot get at it.

956
01:05:42,410 --> 01:05:47,569
The savage, beautiful creature, if I tear, if I rend the slight prison,

957
01:05:48,250 --> 01:05:50,370
my outrage will only let the captive loose.

958
01:05:51,650 --> 01:05:52,650
Conqueror.

959
01:05:53,510 --> 01:05:58,750
I might be of the house, but the inmate would escape to heaven before I could call

960
01:05:58,750 --> 01:06:02,230
myself possessor of its clay dwelling place.

961
01:06:03,169 --> 01:06:10,190
And it is you, spirit, with will and energy, and virtue and purity that I want.

962
01:06:11,050 --> 01:06:12,809
Not alone your brittle frame.

963
01:06:13,930 --> 01:06:17,849
Of yourself you could come with soft flight and nestle against my heart,

964
01:06:18,069 --> 01:06:19,069
if you would.

965
01:06:19,550 --> 01:06:21,029
Seized against your will.

966
01:06:21,889 --> 01:06:24,150
You will elude the grasp like an essence.

967
01:06:25,129 --> 01:06:27,559
You will vanish air I inhale your fragrance.

968
01:06:27,760 --> 01:06:29,260
Oh, calm, Jane, come.

969
01:06:31,260 --> 01:06:36,400
As he said this, he released me from his clutch, and only looked at me.

970
01:06:37,360 --> 01:06:40,080
The look was far worse to resist than the frantic strain.

971
01:06:40,760 --> 01:06:43,260
Only an idiot, however, would have succumbed now.

972
01:06:44,160 --> 01:06:45,860
I had dared and baffled his fury.

973
01:06:46,660 --> 01:06:48,099
I must elude his sorrow.

974
01:06:48,819 --> 01:06:49,919
I retired to the door.

975
01:06:50,720 --> 01:06:51,839
You are going, Jane?

976
01:06:52,660 --> 01:06:53,680
I am going, sir.

977
01:06:54,599 --> 01:06:55,599
You are leaving me.

978
01:06:56,059 --> 01:06:57,059
Yes?

979
01:06:57,199 --> 01:06:58,199
You will not come.

980
01:06:58,360 --> 01:07:02,463
You will not be my comforter, my rescuer, my deep love,

981
01:07:02,463 --> 01:07:06,000
my wild woe, my frantic prayer, are all nothing to you.

982
01:07:07,480 --> 01:07:09,680
What unutterable pathos was in his voice.

983
01:07:10,500 --> 01:07:13,540
How hard it was to reiterate firmly, I am going.

984
01:07:14,279 --> 01:07:18,120
Jane, Mr. Rochester, withdraw then.

985
01:07:18,519 --> 01:07:18,900
I consent.

986
01:07:19,480 --> 01:07:21,919
But remember, you leave me here in anguish.

987
01:07:22,559 --> 01:07:23,559
Go up to your own room.

988
01:07:24,099 --> 01:07:25,620
Think over all I have said.

989
01:07:26,000 --> 01:07:28,900
And Jane cast a glance on my sufferings.

990
01:07:29,440 --> 01:07:30,440
Think of me.

991
01:07:30,839 --> 01:07:31,440
He turned away.

992
01:07:31,639 --> 01:07:33,319
He threw himself on his face on the sofa.

993
01:07:34,680 --> 01:07:39,919
Oh, Jane, my hope, my love, my life, broke in anguish from his lips.

994
01:07:41,199 --> 01:07:43,059
Then came deep, strong sob.

995
01:07:44,040 --> 01:07:47,720
I had already gained the door, but reader, I walked back.

996
01:07:48,839 --> 01:07:52,540
Walked back as determinedly as I had retreated.

997
01:07:53,339 --> 01:07:54,599
I knelt down by him.

998
01:07:55,239 --> 01:07:56,980
I turned his face from the cushion to me.

999
01:07:57,800 --> 01:07:58,800
I kissed his cheek.

1000
01:07:59,319 --> 01:08:01,199
I smoothed his hair with my hand.

1001
01:08:02,379 --> 01:08:04,699
God bless you, my dear master, I said.

1002
01:08:05,660 --> 01:08:08,900
God keep you from harm and wrong, direct you, solace

1003
01:08:08,902 --> 01:08:11,400
you, reward you well for your past kindness to me.

1004
01:08:13,019 --> 01:08:16,480
Little Jane's love would have been my best reward, he answered.

1005
01:08:17,300 --> 01:08:21,300
Without it, my heart is broken, but Jane will give me her love.

1006
01:08:22,379 --> 01:08:24,540
Yes, norbly, generously.

1007
01:08:25,860 --> 01:08:29,839
Up the blood rushed to his face, fourth flash the fire from his eyes,

1008
01:08:30,419 --> 01:08:33,860
erect, he sprang, he held his arms out, but I

1009
01:08:33,860 --> 01:08:37,080
evaded the embrace, and at once quitted the room.

1010
01:08:37,900 --> 01:08:42,040
Farewell was the cry of my heart as I left him, despair added.

1011
01:08:43,440 --> 01:08:44,440
Farewell forever.

1012
01:08:45,760 --> 01:08:48,741
That night I never thought to sleep, but a

1013
01:08:48,741 --> 01:08:52,300
slumber fell on me as soon as I lay down in bed.

1014
01:08:52,760 --> 01:08:56,260
I was transported in thought to the scenes of childhood.

1015
01:08:56,980 --> 01:09:01,500
I dreamt I lay in the red room at Gateshead, that the night was dark,

1016
01:09:02,360 --> 01:09:04,900
and my mind impressed with strange fears.

1017
01:09:05,760 --> 01:09:11,760
The light that long ago had struck me into syncopy, recalled in this vision,

1018
01:09:12,400 --> 01:09:16,057
seemed glidingly to mount the wall, and tremblingly

1019
01:09:16,059 --> 01:09:19,099
to pause in the centre of the obscured ceiling.

1020
01:09:20,099 --> 01:09:21,519
I lifted up my head to look.

1021
01:09:22,459 --> 01:09:27,152
The roof resolved to clouds high and dim, the gleam was

1022
01:09:27,152 --> 01:09:30,739
such as the moon in parts to vapors she is about to sever.

1023
01:09:31,760 --> 01:09:38,559
I watched her come, watched with the strangest anticipation, as though some

1024
01:09:38,561 --> 01:09:41,099
word of doom were to be written on her disc.

1025
01:09:41,699 --> 01:09:45,180
She broke forth as never moon yet burst from cloud.

1026
01:09:45,980 --> 01:09:50,440
A hand first penetrated the sable folds and waved them away.

1027
01:09:51,080 --> 01:09:55,127
Then, not a moon, but a white human form shone in

1028
01:09:55,127 --> 01:09:58,959
the azure, inclining a glorious brow earthward.

1029
01:09:59,779 --> 01:10:01,559
It gazed and gazed on me.

1030
01:10:02,400 --> 01:10:03,819
It spoke to my spirit.

1031
01:10:04,720 --> 01:10:10,379
Immeasurably distant was the tone, yet so near it whispered in my heart.

1032
01:10:11,220 --> 01:10:16,080
My daughter, flea temptation, mother I will.

1033
01:10:17,379 --> 01:10:20,919
So I answered after I had waked from the trance-like dream.

1034
01:10:22,120 --> 01:10:25,239
It was yet night, but July nights are short.

1035
01:10:26,019 --> 01:10:28,739
Soon after midnight dawn comes.

1036
01:10:30,059 --> 01:10:33,080
It cannot be too early to commence the task I have to fulfil.

1037
01:10:33,860 --> 01:10:39,419
Thought I, I rose, I was dressed, for I had taken off nothing but my shoes.

1038
01:10:40,480 --> 01:10:44,900
I knew where to find in my drawers some linen, a locket, a ring.

1039
01:10:45,879 --> 01:10:50,720
In seeking these articles, I encountered the beads of a pearl necklace.

1040
01:10:51,300 --> 01:10:54,599
Mr. Rochester had forced me to accept a few days ago.

1041
01:10:55,519 --> 01:10:56,519
I left that.

1042
01:10:57,180 --> 01:10:58,180
It was not mine.

1043
01:10:59,099 --> 01:11:01,980
It was the visionary brides who had melted in air.

1044
01:11:03,040 --> 01:11:04,760
The other articles I made up in a parcel.

1045
01:11:05,440 --> 01:11:09,220
My purse, containing 20 shillings, it was all I had.

1046
01:11:09,980 --> 01:11:10,980
I put in my pocket.

1047
01:11:11,699 --> 01:11:16,160
I tied on my straw bonnet, pinned my shawl, took the parcel and my slippers,

1048
01:11:16,800 --> 01:11:19,440
which I would not put on yet and stole from my room.

1049
01:11:21,500 --> 01:11:23,580
Farewell, kind Mrs. Fairfax.

1050
01:11:24,480 --> 01:11:27,199
I whispered, as I glided past her door.

1051
01:11:28,239 --> 01:11:33,120
Farewell, my darling Adele, I said, as I glanced towards the nursery.

1052
01:11:34,180 --> 01:11:37,360
No thought could be admitted of entering to embrace her.

1053
01:11:38,459 --> 01:11:43,519
I had to deceive a fine ear, for ought I knew it might now be listening.

1054
01:11:44,660 --> 01:11:48,000
I would have got past Mr. Rochester's chamber without a pause.

1055
01:11:49,180 --> 01:11:52,188
But my heart momentarily stopping its beat at

1056
01:11:52,188 --> 01:11:55,860
that threshold, my foot was forced to stop also.

1057
01:11:56,519 --> 01:11:57,580
No sleep was there.

1058
01:11:58,319 --> 01:12:01,777
The inmate was walking restlessly from wall to wall,

1059
01:12:01,777 --> 01:12:04,480
and again and again he sighed while I listened.

1060
01:12:05,639 --> 01:12:10,739
There was a heaven, a temporary heaven, in this room for me if I chose.

1061
01:12:11,680 --> 01:12:17,739
I had but to go in and to say, Mr. Rochester, I will love you and live

1062
01:12:17,741 --> 01:12:23,781
with you through life till death, and a fount of rapture would spring to my lips.

1063
01:12:23,940 --> 01:12:24,940
I thought of this.

1064
01:12:25,779 --> 01:12:31,419
That kind master who could not sleep now was waiting with impatience for day.

1065
01:12:32,360 --> 01:12:35,019
He would send for me in the morning, I should be gone.

1066
01:12:35,860 --> 01:12:38,059
He would have me sought for, vainly.

1067
01:12:38,720 --> 01:12:40,680
He would feel himself forsaken.

1068
01:12:41,239 --> 01:12:42,239
His love rejected.

1069
01:12:42,919 --> 01:12:43,919
He would suffer.

1070
01:12:44,199 --> 01:12:45,819
Perhaps grow desperate.

1071
01:12:46,559 --> 01:12:47,620
I thought of this too.

1072
01:12:48,419 --> 01:12:50,279
My hand moved towards the lock.

1073
01:12:50,819 --> 01:12:53,059
I caught it back and glided on.

1074
01:12:54,779 --> 01:12:57,279
Drierily, I wound my way downstairs.

1075
01:12:57,980 --> 01:13:00,419
I knew what I had to do, and I did it mechanically.

1076
01:13:01,120 --> 01:13:03,139
I sought the key of the side door in the kitchen.

1077
01:13:04,099 --> 01:13:06,879
I sought, too, a file of oil and a feather.

1078
01:13:07,699 --> 01:13:09,480
I oiled the key and the lock.

1079
01:13:10,300 --> 01:13:11,300
I got some water.

1080
01:13:11,459 --> 01:13:12,459
I got some bread.

1081
01:13:12,980 --> 01:13:15,120
For perhaps I should have to walk far.

1082
01:13:15,760 --> 01:13:20,440
And my strength, sorely shaken of late, must not break down.

1083
01:13:21,139 --> 01:13:23,819
All this I did without one sound.

1084
01:13:24,440 --> 01:13:31,360
I opened the door, passed out, shut it softly, dimmed on and glimmered in the yard.

1085
01:13:31,519 --> 01:13:36,341
The great gates were closed and locked, but a wicked in one of them was only latched.

1086
01:13:36,519 --> 01:13:37,819
Through that, I departed.

1087
01:13:38,260 --> 01:13:39,300
It, too, I shut.

1088
01:13:39,959 --> 01:13:42,400
And now I was out of thornfield.

1089
01:13:43,459 --> 01:13:46,622
A mile off, beyond the fields, lay a road which

1090
01:13:46,622 --> 01:13:49,559
stretched in the contrary direction to milk-coat.

1091
01:13:50,260 --> 01:13:54,639
A road I had never traveled, but often noticed, and wondered where it led.

1092
01:13:55,620 --> 01:13:57,139
The other I bent my steps.

1093
01:13:58,199 --> 01:14:00,260
No reflection was to be allowed now.

1094
01:14:01,059 --> 01:14:02,919
Not one glance was to be cast back.

1095
01:14:03,620 --> 01:14:04,800
Not even one forward.

1096
01:14:05,480 --> 01:14:09,080
Not one thought was to be given either to the past or the future.

1097
01:14:09,879 --> 01:14:17,000
The first was a page so heavenly sweet, so deadly sad, that to read one line of it

1098
01:14:17,000 --> 01:14:20,379
would dissolve my courage and break down my energy.

1099
01:14:21,540 --> 01:14:23,639
The last was an awful blank.

1100
01:14:24,760 --> 01:14:28,540
Something like the world, when the deluge was gone by.

1101
01:14:29,959 --> 01:14:33,919
I skirted fields and hedges and lanes till after sunrise.

1102
01:14:34,819 --> 01:14:37,400
I believe it was a lovely summer morning.

1103
01:14:38,419 --> 01:14:44,260
I know my shoes, which I had put on when I left the house, were soon wet with dew.

1104
01:14:45,319 --> 01:14:50,059
But I looked neither to rising sun or smiling sky nor wakening nature.

1105
01:14:51,160 --> 01:14:56,379
He who is taken out to pass through a fair scene to the scaffold thinks not of the

1106
01:14:56,381 --> 01:15:00,900
flowers that smile on his road, but of the block and axe edge,

1107
01:15:01,400 --> 01:15:07,040
of the disseverment of bone and vein, of the grave gaping at the end.

1108
01:15:07,800 --> 01:15:10,959
And I thought of drear flight and homeless wandering.

1109
01:15:11,699 --> 01:15:16,519
And oh, with agony I thought of what I left, I could not help it.

1110
01:15:17,059 --> 01:15:22,519
I thought of him now, in his room, watching the sunrise, hoping I should soon

1111
01:15:22,521 --> 01:15:24,940
come to say I would stay with him and be his.

1112
01:15:26,019 --> 01:15:27,239
I longed to be his.

1113
01:15:27,879 --> 01:15:28,879
I panted to return.

1114
01:15:29,760 --> 01:15:31,059
It was not too late.

1115
01:15:32,180 --> 01:15:34,720
I could yet spare him the bitter pang of bereavement.

1116
01:15:35,680 --> 01:15:38,400
As yet my flight, I was sure, was undiscovered.

1117
01:15:38,980 --> 01:15:41,040
I could go back and be his comforter.

1118
01:15:42,059 --> 01:15:43,059
His bride.

1119
01:15:43,500 --> 01:15:45,720
His redeemer from misery, perhaps from ruin.

1120
01:15:46,480 --> 01:15:49,300
Oh, that fear of his self-abandonment.

1121
01:15:49,879 --> 01:15:52,180
Far worse than my abandonment.

1122
01:15:52,580 --> 01:15:53,580
How it goaded me.

1123
01:15:54,379 --> 01:15:56,559
It was a barbed arrowhead in my breast.

1124
01:15:57,300 --> 01:15:59,120
It tore me when I tried to extract it.

1125
01:15:59,680 --> 01:16:02,819
It sickened me when remembrance thrust it farther in.

1126
01:16:03,800 --> 01:16:06,160
Birds began singing in break and cops.

1127
01:16:07,360 --> 01:16:09,019
Birds were faithful to their mates.

1128
01:16:10,040 --> 01:16:11,440
Birds were emblems of love.

1129
01:16:12,339 --> 01:16:13,440
What was I?

1130
01:16:14,180 --> 01:16:19,620
In the midst of my pain of heart and frantic effort of principle, I abhorred myself.

1131
01:16:20,279 --> 01:16:22,599
I had no solace from self-approbation.

1132
01:16:23,339 --> 01:16:27,980
None even from self-respect, I had injured, wounded, left my master.

1133
01:16:28,319 --> 01:16:29,879
I was hateful in my own eyes.

1134
01:16:30,559 --> 01:16:34,459
Still, I could not turn, nor retrace one step.

1135
01:16:35,059 --> 01:16:36,239
God must have led me on.

1136
01:16:37,459 --> 01:16:40,141
As to my own will or conscience, in passion

1137
01:16:40,142 --> 01:16:42,720
grief had trampled one and stifled the other.

1138
01:16:43,080 --> 01:16:46,419
I was weeping wildly as I walked along my solitary way.

1139
01:16:47,139 --> 01:16:49,739
Fast, fast, I went, like one delirious.

1140
01:16:50,580 --> 01:16:56,860
A weakness, beginning inwardly, extending to the limbs, seized me, and I fell.

1141
01:16:57,099 --> 01:17:01,540
I lay on the ground some minutes, pressing my face to the wet turf.

1142
01:17:02,419 --> 01:17:06,779
I had some fear, or hope, that here I should die.

1143
01:17:07,919 --> 01:17:12,779
But I was soon up, crawling forwards on my hands and knees, and then again raised to

1144
01:17:12,781 --> 01:17:17,400
my feet, as eager and as determined as ever to reach the road.

1145
01:17:18,300 --> 01:17:23,980
When I got there, I was forced to sit, to rest me under the hedge, and while I

1146
01:17:23,980 --> 01:17:27,720
sat, I heard wheels, and saw a coach come on.

1147
01:17:28,580 --> 01:17:31,440
I stood up and lifted my hand, it stopped.

1148
01:17:32,500 --> 01:17:36,633
I asked where it was going, the driver named a place a long

1149
01:17:36,633 --> 01:17:40,220
way off, and where I was sure Mr. Rochester had no connections.

1150
01:17:41,500 --> 01:17:43,919
I asked for what some he would take me there.

1151
01:17:44,900 --> 01:17:46,319
He said 30 shillings.

1152
01:17:46,779 --> 01:17:48,760
I answered I had but 20.

1153
01:17:49,639 --> 01:17:51,959
Well, he would try to make it do.

1154
01:17:52,760 --> 01:17:56,620
He further gave me leave to get into the inside, as the vehicle was empty.

1155
01:17:57,339 --> 01:18:00,879
I entered, was shut in, and it rolled on its way.

1156
01:18:02,800 --> 01:18:06,360
Gentle reader, may you never feel what I then felt.

1157
01:18:07,400 --> 01:18:13,480
May your eyes never shed such stormy, scolding heart-rung tears as poured from mine.

1158
01:18:13,940 --> 01:18:17,120
May you never appeal to heaven in prayers, so

1159
01:18:17,120 --> 01:18:21,180
hopeless and so agonized as in that hour left my lips.

1160
01:18:22,239 --> 01:18:29,000
For never may you, like me, dread to be the instrument of evil to what you wholly love.
